{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "_DEFAULT_EPSILON = 1e-12\n\ndef truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Given a positive floating point number, return its decimal part.\n    This handles floating-point artifacts by normalizing tiny negative or near-one fractions to 0.0.\n    \"\"\"\n    integer_part = int(number)\n    raw_fraction = number - integer_part\n\n    # Normalize fraction within a small epsilon to handle representation artifacts.\n    if -_DEFAULT_EPSILON < raw_fraction < 0.0:\n        return 0.0\n    # If the fractional part is very close to 1.0, interpret it as an integer and return 0.0.\n    if (1.0 - _DEFAULT_EPSILON) <= raw_fraction < (1.0 + _DEFAULT_EPSILON):\n        return 0.0\n    \n    return raw_fraction"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "import math\n\ndef truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Returns the fractional part of a positive floating-point number.\n    It decomposes the number into an integer part and decimals.\n    \"\"\"\n    integer_part = math.floor(number)\n    decimal = number - integer_part\n    # Normalize tiny negative values that can arise from floating point arithmetic\n    if decimal < 0:\n        decimal = 0.0\n    return round(decimal, 15)"}
