{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the deepest nesting level of parentheses for each space-separated group.\n    Assumes each group contains only valid and balanced parentheses.\n    \"\"\"\n    results: List[int] = []\n    groups = paren_string.split()\n\n    for group in groups:\n        current_depth = 0\n        max_depth = 0\n        for char in group:\n            if char == '(':\n                current_depth += 1\n                if current_depth > max_depth:\n                    max_depth = current_depth\n            else:  # Trusting input, this must be ')'\n                current_depth -= 1\n        results.append(max_depth)\n\n    return results"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of integers, return a tuple consisting of a sum and a product.\n    Empty list sum is 0, empty list product is 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    current_product = 1\n    for number in numbers:\n        current_sum += number\n        current_product *= number\n    return (current_sum, current_product)\n```"}
