n# {\"matches\":[\"hello world\",\"world peace\"],\"count\":2}\n```\n\nFilter strings from a file:\n\n```bash\n# content of input.txt:\n# hello\n# world\n# hello world\n# another string\n# world peace\n\nstrfilter --substring \"world\" --input-file input.txt\n# Output:\n# {\"matches\":[\"world\",\"hello world\",\"world peace\"],\"count\":3}\n```\n\nCase-insensitive filtering:\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"hello\" --input \"Hello World\" \"hello there\" --case-insensitive\n# Output:\n# {\"matches\":[\"Hello World\",\"hello there\"],\"count\":2}\n```\n\nPersist requests to a history file (`strfilter_history.json` by default):\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"test\" --input \"test1\" \"test2\" --persist\n```\n\n## HTTP API Usage\n\nThe HTTP API runs on `http://127.0.0.1:8000` by default.\n\nTo start the API server:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn strfilter.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nExample `POST /filter` request:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"strings\": [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"grape\", \"orange\"],\n           \"substring\": \"ap\",\n           \"persist\": true,\n           \"case_insensitive\": false\n         }'\n```\n\nExample response:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\"apple\", \"grape\"],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\n## Development\n\nClone the repository and install development dependencies:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/strfilter.git\ncd strfilter\npip install -e .[dev]\n```\n\nRun tests:\n\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\nRefer to the design specification for details on modularity, layers, and components.\n```\n\n```python\n# .gitignore\n# Python\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n*.pyo\n*.pyd\n.Python\nenv/\nvenv/\n.venv/\n.mypy_cache/\n.pytest_cache/\n.vscode/\n\n# Editor\n.idea/\n\n# OS\n.DS_Store\nThumbs.db\n\n# Logs & History\nstrfilter_history.json\n```\n\n```python\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI/CD Pipeline\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: |\n        python -m pip install --upgrade pip\n        pip install .[dev]\n    - name: Lint with Flake8\n      run: |\n        pip install flake8\n        flake8 src tests\n    - name: Type check with MyPy\n      run: |\n        pip install mypy\n        mypy src\n    - name: Run tests with Pytest\n      run: |\n        pytest\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nstrfilter package: Provides a reusable library, CLI, and HTTP API for filtering lists of strings.\n\"\"\"\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/exceptions.py\n\"\"\"\nDomain-specific exceptions for the strfilter application.\n\"\"\"\n\nclass FilterError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for strfilter related errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass ValidationError(FilterError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input or request data.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass PersistenceError(FilterError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for errors during data persistence operations.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/models.py\n\"\"\"\nPydantic models for request and response data transfer objects (DTOs).\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import List\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass FilterRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents an incoming filter request.\"\"\"\n    strings: List[str] = Field(..., min_length=0, description=\"List of strings to filter.\")\n    substring: str = Field(..., min_length=1, description=\"Substring to search for.\")\n    persist: bool = Field(False, description=\"Whether to persist the request and result.\")\n    case_insensitive: bool = Field(False, description=\"Whether to perform case-insensitive matching.\")\n\nclass FilterResult(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a filter operation.\"\"\"\n    matches: List[str] = Field(..., description=\"List of strings that matched the substring.\")\n    count: int = Field(..., description=\"Number of matched strings.\")\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_matches(cls, matches: List[str]) -> \"FilterResult\":\n        \"\"\"Creates a FilterResult from a list of matches.\"\"\"\n        return cls(matches=matches, count=len(matches))\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/utils.py\n\"\"\"\nUtility functions and classes for validation and JSON handling.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport threading\nfrom typing import Any, List\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\n\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"Provides utility methods for input validation.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def ensure_list_of_str(value: Any, name: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the value is a list containing only strings.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(value, list):\n            raise ValidationError(f\"'{name}' must be a list.\")\n        for item in value:\n            if not isinstance(item, str):\n                raise ValidationError(f\"All elements in '{name}' must be strings.\")\n        return value\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def ensure_substring(value: Any) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the value is a non-empty string.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Substring must be a string.\")\n        if not value:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Substring cannot be empty.\")\n        return value\n\nclass JSONWriter:\n    \"\"\"Utility for safely appending JSON objects to a file as newline-delimited JSON.\"\"\"\n    _lock = threading.Lock() # Class-level lock for file operations\n\n    @classmethod\n    def append_json_object(cls, path: str, obj: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Appends a JSON object to a file, ensuring thread-safe newline-delimited JSON format.\n        Creates the file if it doesn't exist.\n        \"\"\"\n        with cls._lock:\n            try:\n                # Ensure directory exists\n                os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n                with open(path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    f.write(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n            except IOError as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to write to JSON file '{path}': {e}\") from e\n\n    @classmethod\n    def read_json_lines(cls, path: str, limit: int | None = None) -> List[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Reads newline-delimited JSON objects from a file.\"\"\"\n        records: List[dict] = []\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            return records\n        with cls._lock:\n            try:\n                with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                    # Read lines in reverse for performance when limit is small\n                    lines = f.readlines()\n                    for line in reversed(lines):\n                        line = line.strip()\n                        if line:\n                            records.append(json.loads(line))\n                            if limit is not None and len(records) >= limit:\n                                break\n            except (IOError, json.JSONDecodeError) as e:\n                raise PersistenceError(f\"Failed to read from JSON file '{path}': {e}\") from e\n        return list(reversed(records)) # Return in original chronological order\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/filters.py\n\"\"\"\nPure functions for string filtering operations.\n\"\"\"\nfrom typing import List, Any\nfrom .exceptions import TypeError, ValueError\n\nclass Filters:\n    \"\"\"Provides pure filtering algorithms.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_CASE_INSENSITIVE: bool = False\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def filter_by_substring(strings: List[str], substring: str, case_insensitive: bool = False) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a list of strings that contain the given substring.\n        Preserves original order and string values.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(strings, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'strings' must be a list of str.\")\n        if substring is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input 'substring' must not be None.\")\n        if not isinstance(substring, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 'substring' must be a string.\")\n\n        if case_insensitive:\n            sub = substring.lower()\n            return [s for s in strings if isinstance(s, str) and sub in s.lower()]\n        else:\n            return [s for s in strings if isinstance(s, str) and substring in s]\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/repositories.py\n\"\"\"\nRepository interfaces and implementations for data persistence.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .utils import JSONWriter\nfrom .exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nclass BaseRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class defining the contract for data persistence.\"\"\"\n    @abstractmethod\n    def save(self, record: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves a single record.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def list(self, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of records, optionally limited.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass InMemoryRepository(BaseRepository):\n    \"\"\"An in-memory implementation of BaseRepository for transient storage.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self._store: List[dict] = []\n\n    def save(self, record: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Appends a record to the in-memory store.\"\"\"\n        self._store.append(record)\n\n    def list(self, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Returns stored records, optionally limited to the latest.\"\"\"\n        if limit is None:\n            return list(self._store)\n        return self._store[-limit:]\n\nclass FileRepository(BaseRepository):\n    \"\"\"File-based repository using newline-delimited JSON for persistence.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_PATH: str = \"strfilter_history.json\"\n\n    def __init__(self, path: str = DEFAULT_PATH) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes with a file path for persistence.\"\"\"\n        self.path = path\n\n    def save(self, record: dict) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Saves a record to the configured JSON file.\"\"\"\n        JSONWriter.append_json_object(self.path, record)\n\n    def list(self, limit: Optional[int] = None) -> List[dict]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves records from the JSON file.\"\"\"\n        return JSONWriter.read_json_lines(self.path, limit)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/services.py\n\"\"\"\nApplication service layer orchestrating business logic and interactions.\n\"\"\"\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .filters import Filters\nfrom .repositories import BaseRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom .utils import Validator\n\nclass FilterService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation, filtering, and optional persistence.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, repository: BaseRepository) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the service with a persistence repository.\"\"\"\n        self._repository = repository\n\n    def run(self, request: FilterRequest) -> FilterResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the request, performs filtering, and optionally persists the operation.\n        Returns a FilterResult containing the matches and count.\n        \"\"\"\n        # Pydantic handles initial validation, but _validate adds domain-specific checks.\n        self._validate(request)\n\n        matches = Filters.filter_by_substring(\n            request.strings, request.substring, request.case_insensitive\n        )\n        result = FilterResult.from_matches(matches)\n\n        if request.persist:\n            record = {\n                \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n                \"request\": request.model_dump(), # Use model_dump for Pydantic v2+\n                \"result\": result.model_dump(),\n            }\n            try:\n                self._repository.save(record)\n            except PersistenceError as e:\n                # Log the error, but still return the filter result\n                print(f\"Warning: Persistence failed for request {request.substring}: {e}\")\n                # Depending on config, might re-raise or just log\n                # For now, we'll log and continue if filtering was successful.\n\n        return result\n\n    def _validate(self, request: FilterRequest) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Performs additional domain-specific validation beyond Pydantic's.\"\"\"\n        # Pydantic's validation takes care of list[str] and non-empty substring\n        # For simplicity, we can rely on Pydantic's robust validation for `FilterRequest`\n        # and let it raise `ValidationError` if types/constraints are violated.\n        # This method could be extended for more complex business rules.\n        pass # Pydantic model validation handles most of this.\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/cli.py\n\"\"\"\nCommand-Line Interface (CLI) entrypoint using the `click` library.\n\"\"\"\nimport click\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .services import FilterService\nfrom .repositories import InMemoryRepository, FileRepository\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError, ValidationError\n\n# Environment variable for history file path\nHISTORY_PATH_ENV_VAR = \"STRFILTER_HISTORY_PATH\"\n\n@click.command()\n@click.option(\n    \"--substring\",\n    required=True,\n    help=\"The substring to filter by.\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--input\",\n    \"input_strings\",\n    multiple=True,\n    help=\"Individual strings to filter. Can be specified multiple times.\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--input-file\",\n    type=click.Path(exists=True),\n    help=\"Path to a file containing strings (one per line) to filter.\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--persist\",\n    is_flag=True,\n    help=\"If set, the request and result will be persisted to a history file.\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--case-insensitive\",\n    is_flag=True,\n    help=\"Perform case-insensitive substring matching.\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--json-output\",\n    is_flag=True,\n    default=True, # Default to JSON output\n    help=\"Output results as JSON (default).\"\n)\n@click.option(\n    \"--plain-output\",\n    is_flag=True,\n    default=False,\n    help=\"Output matched strings as plain text, one per line.\"\n)\ndef main(\n    substring: str,\n    input_strings: List[str],\n    input_file: Optional[str],\n    persist: bool,\n    case_insensitive: bool,\n    json_output: bool,\n    plain_output: bool,\n) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of strings by a given substring, providing CLI access.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        strings_to_filter: List[str] = list(input_strings)\n\n        if input_file:\n            with open(input_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                strings_to_filter.extend([line.strip() for line in f if line.strip()])\n\n        if not strings_to_filter:\n            click.echo(\"Error: No input strings provided. Use --input or --input-file.\", err=True)\n            return 1\n\n        # Determine which repository to use based on 'persist' flag and environment\n        if persist:\n            history_path = os.getenv(HISTORY_PATH_ENV_VAR, FileRepository.DEFAULT_PATH)\n            repository = FileRepository(path=history_path)\n        else:\n            repository = InMemoryRepository()\n\n        service = FilterService(repository=repository)\n\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=strings_to_filter,\n            substring=substring,\n            persist=persist,\n            case_insensitive=case_insensitive,\n        )\n\n        result: FilterResult = service.run(request)\n\n        if plain_output:\n            for match in result.matches:\n                click.echo(match)\n        else: # Default to JSON output\n            click.echo(result.model_dump_json(indent=2))\n\n        return 0\n\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        click.echo(f\"Validation Error: {e}\", err=True)\n        return 2 # Exit code for validation errors\n    except FilterError as e:\n        click.echo(f\"Filter Error: {e}\", err=True)\n        return 1\n    except Exception as e:\n        click.echo(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", err=True)\n        return 1\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    exit(main()) # pragma: no cover\n```\n\n```python\n# src/strfilter/api.py\n\"\"\"\nFastAPI application for the HTTP API endpoint.\n\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport uvicorn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\n\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, status\nfrom pydantic import ValidationError as PydanticValidationError\n\nfrom .models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom .services import FilterService\nfrom .repositories import FileRepository, InMemoryRepository\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\n\n# Environment variable for history file path\nHISTORY_PATH_ENV_VAR = \"STRFILTER_HISTORY_PATH\"\n\ndef create_app() -> FastAPI:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates and configures the FastAPI application.\n    \"\"\"\n    app = FastAPI(\n        title=\"Substring Filter API\",\n        description=\"HTTP API for filtering lists of strings by substring.\",\n        version=\"0.1.0\",\n    )\n\n    # Initialize repository\n    history_path = os.getenv(HISTORY_PATH_ENV_VAR, FileRepository.DEFAULT_PATH)\n    # Using FileRepository for the API so persistence works\n    repository = FileRepository(path=history_path)\n    filter_service = FilterService(repository=repository)\n\n    @app.post(\"/filter\", response_model=FilterResult, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n    async def filter_strings_endpoint(request: FilterRequest) -> FilterResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Filters a list of strings by a substring based on the provided request body.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            result = filter_service.run(request)\n            return result\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e)) from e\n        except PersistenceError as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=f\"Persistence error: {e}\") from e\n        except PydanticValidationError as e:\n            # Pydantic's own validation errors for request body\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_422_UNPROCESSABLE_ENTITY, detail=e.errors()) from e\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=f\"Internal server error: {e}\") from e\n\n    return app\n\napp = create_app() # This is the app instance uvicorn will run\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # For local development: python -m strfilter.api\n    host = os.getenv(\"STRFILTER_HOST\", \"127.0.0.1\")\n    port = int(os.getenv(\"STRFILTER_PORT\", \"8000\"))\n    uvicorn.run(app, host=host, port=port) # pragma: no cover\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_filters.py\nimport pytest\nfrom src.strfilter.filters import Filters\nfrom src.strfilter.exceptions import TypeError, ValueError\n\nclass TestFilters:\n    def test_empty_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with an empty list of strings.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring([], 'a') == []\n\n    def test_no_matches(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with no matching strings.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['bcd', 'def'], 'a') == []\n\n    def test_single_match(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with a single matching string.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['abc'], 'a') == ['abc']\n\n    def test_multiple_matches(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with multiple matching strings, preserving order.\"\"\"\n        strings = ['abc', 'bacd', 'cde', 'array', 'sub']\n        expected = ['abc', 'bacd', 'array']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, 'a') == expected\n\n    def test_substring_at_start(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with substring at the beginning.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['apple', 'banana'], 'ap') == ['apple']\n\n    def test_substring_at_end(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with substring at the end.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['apple', 'grape'], 'pe') == ['apple', 'grape']\n\n    def test_case_sensitive_default(self):\n        \"\"\"Test default case-sensitive behavior.\"\"\"\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['Hello', 'hello'], 'Hello') == ['Hello']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(['Hello', 'hello'], 'hello') == ['hello']\n\n    def test_case_insensitive_option(self):\n        \"\"\"Test case-insensitive matching.\"\"\"\n        strings = ['Hello World', 'hello there', 'WORLD peace']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, 'hello', case_insensitive=True) == ['Hello World', 'hello there']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, 'world', case_insensitive=True) == ['Hello World', 'WORLD peace']\n\n    def test_empty_substring(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with an empty substring, should match all (as per string.find behavior).\"\"\"\n        strings = ['abc', 'def']\n        expected = ['abc', 'def']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, '') == expected\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, '', case_insensitive=True) == expected\n\n    def test_non_string_elements_in_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with mixed types in the input list, only strings should be processed.\"\"\"\n        strings = ['test1', 123, 'test2', None, 'test3'] # type: ignore\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, 'test') == ['test1', 'test2', 'test3']\n        assert Filters.filter_by_substring(strings, 'test', case_insensitive=True) == ['test1', 'test2', 'test3']\n\n    def test_strings_is_none_raises_type_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that passing None for strings raises TypeError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Input 'strings' must be a list of str\"):\n            Filters.filter_by_substring(None, 'a') # type: ignore\n\n    def test_strings_is_not_list_raises_type_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that passing non-list for strings raises TypeError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Input 'strings' must be a list of str\"):\n            Filters.filter_by_substring(\"not a list\", 'a') # type: ignore\n\n    def test_substring_is_none_raises_value_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that passing None for substring raises ValueError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Input 'substring' must not be None\"):\n            Filters.filter_by_substring(['a'], None) # type: ignore\n\n    def test_substring_is_not_string_raises_type_error(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that passing non-string for substring raises TypeError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(TypeError, match=\"Input 'substring' must be a string.\"):\n            Filters.filter_by_substring(['a'], 123) # type: ignore\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_service.py\nimport pytest\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock, patch\n\nfrom src.strfilter.services import FilterService\nfrom src.strfilter.models import FilterRequest, FilterResult\nfrom src.strfilter.exceptions import ValidationError, PersistenceError\nfrom src.strfilter.repositories import BaseRepository, InMemoryRepository\n\nclass TestFilterService:\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def mock_repository(self) -> MagicMock:\n        \"\"\"Fixture for a mocked repository.\"\"\"\n        repo = MagicMock(spec=BaseRepository)\n        repo.save.return_value = None\n        repo.list.return_value = []\n        return repo\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def in_memory_repository(self) -> InMemoryRepository:\n        \"\"\"Fixture for an in-memory repository.\"\"\"\n        return InMemoryRepository()\n\n    def test_run_success_no_persist(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test successful run without persistence.\"\"\"\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[\"apple\", \"banana\", \"grape\"],\n            substring=\"ap\",\n            persist=False\n        )\n        result = service.run(request)\n\n        assert result.matches == [\"apple\", \"grape\"]\n        assert result.count == 2\n        mock_repository.save.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_run_success_with_persist(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test successful run with persistence.\"\"\"\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[\"apple\", \"banana\", \"grape\"],\n            substring=\"ap\",\n            persist=True,\n            case_insensitive=False\n        )\n        \n        # Patch datetime.now() for predictable timestamp in record\n        with patch('src.strfilter.services.datetime') as mock_dt:\n            mock_dt.now.return_value = datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, 0)\n            mock_dt.now.isoformat.return_value = \"2023-01-01T12:00:00\"\n\n            result = service.run(request)\n\n            assert result.matches == [\"apple\", \"grape\"]\n            assert result.count == 2\n            mock_repository.save.assert_called_once()\n            \n            # Check the structure of the saved record\n            saved_record = mock_repository.save.call_args[0][0]\n            assert \"timestamp\" in saved_record\n            assert saved_record[\"timestamp\"] == \"2023-01-01T12:00:00\"\n            assert \"request\" in saved_record\n            assert saved_record[\"request\"] == request.model_dump()\n            assert \"result\" in saved_record\n            assert saved_record[\"result\"] == result.model_dump()\n\n    def test_run_case_insensitive(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test case-insensitive filtering.\"\"\"\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[\"Apple\", \"banana\", \"Grape\"],\n            substring=\"ap\",\n            persist=False,\n            case_insensitive=True\n        )\n        result = service.run(request)\n        assert result.matches == [\"Apple\", \"Grape\"]\n        assert result.count == 2\n        mock_repository.save.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_run_no_matches(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test scenario with no matches.\"\"\"\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[\"apple\", \"banana\"],\n            substring=\"xyz\",\n            persist=False\n        )\n        result = service.run(request)\n        assert result.matches == []\n        assert result.count == 0\n        mock_repository.save.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_empty_strings_list(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test with an empty input strings list.\"\"\"\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[],\n            substring=\"a\",\n            persist=False\n        )\n        result = service.run(request)\n        assert result.matches == []\n        assert result.count == 0\n        mock_repository.save.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_repository_persistence_error_handling(self, mock_repository: MagicMock):\n        \"\"\"Test that PersistenceError is caught and logged, but filter result is still returned.\"\"\"\n        mock_repository.save.side_effect = PersistenceError(\"Write failed\")\n        service = FilterService(repository=mock_repository)\n        request = FilterRequest(\n            strings=[\"test\"],\n            substring=\"t\",\n            persist=True\n        )\n\n        with patch('builtins.print') as mock_print: # Capture print statements for logging\n            result = service.run(request)\n            \n            assert result.matches == [\"test\"]\n            assert result.count == 1\n            mock_repository.save.assert_called_once()\n            mock_print.assert_called_once_with(f\"Warning: Persistence failed for request {request.substring}: Write failed\")\n\n    # Test cases for pydantic validation errors, which are not directly raised by FilterService.run\n    # but caught by higher layers (e.g., API controller). Here we just test what happens if pydantic\n    # *allows* something invalid, which shouldn't happen with current models.\n    # The _validate method in FilterService is currently a pass-through, relying on Pydantic.\n    # If it were to be extended, this would be the place to test it.\n    \n    # Example of how pydantic validation would be triggered before service.run()\n    def test_pydantic_validation_invalid_substring(self):\n        \"\"\"Test Pydantic validation for invalid substring.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(PydanticValidationError):\n            FilterRequest(strings=[\"a\"], substring=\"\") # min_length=1 constraint\n        \n        with pytest.raises(PydanticValidationError):\n            FilterRequest(strings=[\"a\"], substring=None) # type: ignore\n\n    def test_pydantic_validation_invalid_strings_type(self):\n        \"\"\"Test Pydantic validation for invalid strings type.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(PydanticValidationError):\n            FilterRequest(strings=\"not a list\", substring=\"a\") # type: ignore\n        \n        with pytest.raises(PydanticValidationError):\n            FilterRequest(strings=[123, \"a\"], substring=\"a\") # type: ignore\n```\n\n```python\n# tests/test_repositories.py\nimport pytest\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nimport json\nfrom src.strfilter.repositories import InMemoryRepository, FileRepository\nfrom src.strfilter.exceptions import PersistenceError\n\nclass TestInMemoryRepository:\n    def test_save_and_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Test saving and listing records in InMemoryRepository.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryRepository()\n        record1 = {\"id\": 1, \"data\": \"first\"}\n        record2 = {\"id\": 2, \"data\": \"second\"}\n\n        repo.save(record1)\n        assert repo.list() == [record1]\n\n        repo.save(record2)\n        assert repo.list() == [record1, record2]\n\n    def test_list_with_limit(self):\n        \"\"\"Test listing records with a limit.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryRepository()\n        for i in range(5):\n            repo.save({\"id\": i})\n\n        assert len(repo.list()) == 5\n        assert repo.list(limit=2) == [{\"id\": 3}, {\"id\": 4}]\n        assert repo.list(limit=10) == [{\"id\": 0}, {\"id\": 1}, {\"id\": 2}, {\"id\": 3}, {\"id\": 4}]\n        assert repo.list(limit=0) == []\n\n    def test_empty_repository(self):\n        \"\"\"Test listing from an empty repository.\"\"\"\n        repo = InMemoryRepository()\n        assert repo.list() == []\n        assert repo.list(limit=5) == []\n\nclass TestFileRepository:\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def temp_file_path(self):\n        \"\"\"Fixture to provide a temporary file path.\"\"\"\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmpdir:\n            yield os.path.join(tmpdir, \"test_history.json\")\n\n    def test_save_and_list(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test saving and listing records in FileRepository.\"\"\"\n        repo = FileRepository(path=temp_file_path)\n        record1 = {\"id\": 1, \"data\": \"first\", \"timestamp\": \"2023-01-01T10:00:00\"}\n        record2 = {\"id\": 2, \"data\": \"second\", \"timestamp\": \"2023-01-01T10:01:00\"}\n\n        repo.save(record1)\n        assert os.path.exists(temp_file_path)\n        \n        # Verify file content\n        with open(temp_file_path, 'r') as f:\n            lines = f.readlines()\n            assert len(lines) == 1\n            assert json.loads(lines[0]) == record1\n\n        repo.save(record2)\n        with open(temp_file_path, 'r') as f:\n            lines = f.readlines()\n            assert len(lines) == 2\n            assert json.loads(lines[0]) == record1\n            assert json.loads(lines[1]) == record2\n\n        assert repo.list() == [record1, record2]\n\n    def test_list_with_limit(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test listing records with a limit from file.\"\"\"\n        repo = FileRepository(path=temp_file_path)\n        records = []\n        for i in range(5):\n            record = {\"id\": i, \"timestamp\": f\"2023-01-01T10:0{i}:00\"}\n            repo.save(record)\n            records.append(record)\n        \n        # List all\n        assert repo.list() == records\n\n        # List with limit\n        assert repo.list(limit=2) == [records[3], records[4]]\n        assert repo.list(limit=3) == [records[2], records[3], records[4]]\n        assert repo.list(limit=10) == records # Limit greater than total records\n\n    def test_empty_file_repository(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test listing from an empty or non-existent file.\"\"\"\n        repo = FileRepository(path=temp_file_path)\n        assert not os.path.exists(temp_file_path)\n        assert repo.list() == []\n        assert repo.list(limit=5) == []\n\n    def test_invalid_json_in_file(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test handling of invalid JSON in the file.\"\"\"\n        with open(temp_file_path, 'w') as f:\n            f.write('{\"id\": 1}\\n')\n            f.write('{\"id\": 2, \"invalid\"\\n') # Corrupted line\n            f.write('{\"id\": 3}\\n')\n\n        repo = FileRepository(path=temp_file_path)\n        with pytest.raises(PersistenceError, match=\"Failed to read from JSON file\"):\n            repo.list()\n\n    def test_save_io_error(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test handling of IOError during saving.\"\"\"\n        # Make path unwritable (e.g., directory doesn't exist and can't be created)\n        # This specific test might be tricky without elevated permissions or mock filesystem\n        # For simplicity, we can mock `open` or try to write to a forbidden path if possible.\n        # Here, we simulate by passing an invalid path (e.g., to a non-writable root)\n        # However, for `FileRepository` to `append_json_object` to raise error, it must fail.\n        # A direct way is to make the directory read-only after creation, or mock.\n        \n        # Let's try to pass a path that's an existing file, but not a directory, \n        # and then try to create a sub-file inside it. This should cause an error.\n        dummy_file = temp_file_path + \".dummy\"\n        with open(dummy_file, \"w\") as f:\n            f.write(\"dummy content\")\n        \n        repo = FileRepository(path=os.path.join(dummy_file, \"sub_file.json\"))\n\n        with pytest.raises(PersistenceError):\n            repo.save({\"test\": \"data\"})\n        \n        os.remove(dummy_file) # Clean up dummy file\n\n    def test_list_io_error(self, temp_file_path: str):\n        \"\"\"Test handling of IOError during listing.\"\"\"\n        repo = FileRepository(path=temp_file_path)\n        # Simulate a permission error by pointing to an inaccessible location\n        # This requires more advanced mocking or specific OS permissions setup,\n        # but for unit testing, we can check for the exception type.\n        \n        # Create a file, then remove read permissions\n        with open(temp_file_path, 'w') as f:\n            f.write('{\"id\": 1}\\n')\n        \n        os.chmod(temp_file_path, 0o000) # Remove all permissions\n        \n        with pytest.raises(PersistenceError):\n            repo.list()\n\n        os.chmod(temp_file_path, 0o644) # Restore permissions for cleanup\n```\n\n```python\n# docs/api_examples.md\n# API Examples\n\nThis document provides quick examples for interacting with the `strfilter` HTTP API and CLI.\n\n---\n\n## HTTP API Examples\n\nThe `strfilter` HTTP API exposes a single endpoint for filtering strings.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /filter`\n**Default Host:** `http://127.0.0.1:8000` (can be configured via `STRFILTER_HOST` and `STRFILTER_PORT`)\n\nTo start the API server:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn strfilter.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\n### 1. Basic Filtering Request\n\nFilters a list of strings for a specified substring.\n\n**Request:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"strings\": [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"grape\", \"orange\"],\n           \"substring\": \"ap\",\n           \"persist\": false,\n           \"case_insensitive\": false\n         }'\n```\n\n**Response (200 OK):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\"apple\", \"grape\"],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Case-Insensitive Filtering\n\nPerforms the search without regard to case.\n\n**Request:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"strings\": [\"Hello World\", \"hello there\", \"WORLD peace\"],\n           \"substring\": \"world\",\n           \"persist\": false,\n           \"case_insensitive\": true\n         }'\n```\n\n**Response (200 OK):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\"Hello World\", \"WORLD peace\"],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Persisting the Request and Result\n\nWhen `persist` is `true`, the request and its corresponding result are saved to the history file (`strfilter_history.json` by default).\n\n**Request:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"strings\": [\"test-string-1\", \"example-test\", \"no-match\"],\n           \"substring\": \"test\",\n           \"persist\": true,\n           \"case_insensitive\": false\n         }'\n```\n\n**Response (200 OK):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\"test-string-1\", \"example-test\"],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\nThe history file (`strfilter_history.json`) would now contain an entry like:\n\n```json\n{\"timestamp\":\"2023-10-27T10:30:00.123456\",\"request\":{\"strings\":[\"test-string-1\",\"example-test\",\"no-match\"],\"substring\":\"test\",\"persist\":true,\"case_insensitive\":false},\"result\":{\"matches\":[\"test-string-1\",\"example-test\"],\"count\":2}}\n```\n\n### 4. Handling Invalid Requests (Validation Error)\n\nSubmitting an invalid payload (e.g., missing required fields, wrong types) will result in a `422 Unprocessable Entity` or `400 Bad Request` error.\n\n**Request (missing `substring`):**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:8000/filter\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"strings\": [\"abc\", \"def\"]\n         }'\n```\n\n**Response (422 Unprocessable Entity):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"missing\",\n      \"loc\": [\"body\", \"substring\"],\n      \"msg\": \"Field required\",\n      \"input\": null,\n      \"url\": \"https://errors.pydantic.dev/2.7/v/missing\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## CLI Examples\n\nThe `strfilter` CLI tool provides direct command-line access to the filtering functionality.\n\n### 1. Basic Filtering from Input Arguments\n\nFilter strings provided directly as command-line arguments.\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"cat\" --input \"my cat is cute\" \"dog and cat\" \"bird song\"\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\n    \"my cat is cute\",\n    \"dog and cat\"\n  ],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Filtering from a File\n\nReads strings from a specified file (one string per line).\n\nFirst, create an `input.txt` file:\n```\napple pie\nbanana bread\ngrape jelly\npineapple juice\n```\n\nThen run the command:\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"pie\" --input-file input.txt\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\n    \"apple pie\"\n  ],\n  \"count\": 1\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Combined Input Arguments and File\n\nYou can mix `--input` arguments with `--input-file`.\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"fruit\" --input \"tropical fruit\" --input-file input.txt\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\n    \"tropical fruit\"\n  ],\n  \"count\": 1\n}\n```\n\n(Assuming `input.txt` did not contain \"fruit\" in this example.)\n\n### 4. Case-Insensitive Matching (CLI)\n\nUse the `--case-insensitive` flag for case-agnostic searches.\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"orange\" --input \"Orange Juice\" \"apple orange\" \"banana\" --case-insensitive\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"matches\": [\n    \"Orange Juice\",\n    \"apple orange\"\n  ],\n  \"count\": 2\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Persisting CLI Requests\n\nUse the `--persist` flag to log CLI requests to the history file.\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"log\" --input \"log this request\" \"another log entry\" --persist\n```\n\nThis will add an entry to `strfilter_history.json`.\n\n### 6. Plain Text Output\n\nUse the `--plain-output` flag to get results as one match per line, without JSON.\n\n```bash\nstrfilter --substring \"a\" --input \"apple\" \"banana\" \"grape\" --plain-output\n```\n\n**Output:**\n\n```\napple\nbanana\ngrape\n```\n```"}
