{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any, List\n\ndef sort_even(l: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the odd indicies, while its values at the even indicies are equal\n    to the values of the even indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    # Extract elements at even indices\n    evens = [l[i] for i in range(0, len(l), 2)]\n    \n    # Sort the extracted even-indexed elements\n    evens_sorted = sorted(evens)\n    \n    # Create a new list, initially a copy of the original\n    result = list(l)\n    \n    # Replace the even-indexed elements in the new list with the sorted ones\n    for idx, val in enumerate(evens_sorted):\n        result[2 * idx] = val\n        \n    return result\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def encode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes a string by cycling groups of three characters.\n    Groups of fewer than three characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    # split string to groups. Each of length 3.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n    # cycle elements in each group. Unless group has fewer elements than 3.\n    groups = [(group[1:] + group[0]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n    return \"\".join(groups)\n\n\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string previously encoded with encode_cyclic.\n    It reverses the cycle for groups of three characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    # split string to groups. Each of length 3.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n    # reverse cycle elements in each group. Unless group has fewer elements than 3.\n    groups = [(group[2] + group[0:2]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n    return \"\".join(groups)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "def encode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Encodes a string by cycling groups of three characters left by one position.\n    Groups shorter than three characters remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n    encoded_groups = [(group[1:] + group[0]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n    return \"\".join(encoded_groups)\n\n\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string that was encoded using encode_cyclic, reversing the character cycle.\n    Groups shorter than three characters are left as they were.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n    decoded_groups = [(group[-1] + group[:-1]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/39", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_fib returns n-th number that is a Fibonacci number and it's also prime.\n    >>> prime_fib(1)\n    2\n    >>> prime_fib(2)\n    3\n    >>> prime_fib(3)\n    5\n    >>> prime_fib(4)\n    13\n    >>> prime_fib(5)\n    89\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function for primality test, defined inline as per requirements.\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2 or num == 3:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    prime_fib_count = 0\n    fib_a, fib_b = 1, 1  # Initialize with F_1 and F_2 of the Fibonacci sequence\n\n    # Iterate through Fibonacci numbers to find the n-th prime one.\n    while True:\n        # Calculate the next Fibonacci number: F_k = F_{k-1} + F_{k-2}\n        next_fib_val = fib_a + fib_b\n        \n        # Update fib_a and fib_b for the next iteration.\n        fib_a, fib_b = fib_b, next_fib_val\n\n        # Check if the current Fibonacci number is prime.\n        if is_prime(next_fib_val):\n            prime_fib_count += 1\n            if prime_fib_count == n:\n                return next_fib_val\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "def triples_sum_to_zero(l: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    It returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    if n < 3:\n        return False\n\n    nums = sorted(l)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        # Prevent checking the same first element multiple times if values are identical.\n        if i > 0 and nums[i] == nums[i - 1]:\n            continue\n\n        left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n        target = -nums[i]\n\n        while left < right:\n            current_sum = nums[left] + nums[right]\n            if current_sum == target:\n                return True\n            elif current_sum < target:\n                left += 1\n            else:\n                right -= 1\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "```\nsrc/triples_sum/__init__.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nTriples Sum to Zero package.\nProvides library functions, CLI, and a REST API to detect if three distinct elements in a list sum to zero.\n\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/config.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nConfiguration constants for the triples_sum application.\nThis module centralizes default settings and paths.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nimport os\n\n# Database configuration\nDB_DIR = \"./data\"\nDB_PATH = os.path.join(DB_DIR, \"triples_sum.db\")\n\n# Algorithm configuration\nDEFAULT_STRATEGY = \"two_pointer\"\nMIN_ITEMS = 3 # Minimum number of items required for evaluation\n\n# Logging configuration\nLOG_LEVEL = logging.INFO\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/models.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nData Transfer Objects (DTOs) for requests and results.\nThese models define the structure of data exchanged within the application.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nclass TriplesRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents an incoming request for triplet evaluation.\"\"\"\n    items: List[int] = Field(..., description=\"List of integers to evaluate.\")\n\nclass TriplesResult(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Represents the result of a triplet evaluation.\"\"\"\n    result: bool = Field(..., description=\"True if a triplet summing to zero was found, False otherwise.\")\n    strategy: str = Field(..., description=\"The algorithm strategy used for evaluation.\")\n    error: Optional[str] = Field(None, description=\"Error message if an exception occurred during evaluation.\")\n    timestamp: datetime = Field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow, description=\"UTC timestamp of when the result was generated.\")\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/external.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nA convenience wrapper to simulate an external caller.\nThis class simplifies interaction with the TriplesService for testing or simple integrations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Optional, List\nfrom .models import TriplesResult\nfrom .services import TriplesService\nfrom .repository import TriplesRepository\nfrom .validators import InputValidator\nfrom .algorithms.factory import StrategyFactory\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_STRATEGY, DB_PATH\n\nclass ExternalCaller:\n    \"\"\"Provides a simple interface to evaluate a list of integers.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the external caller with default service dependencies.\"\"\"\n        repo = TriplesRepository(db_path=DB_PATH)\n        validator = InputValidator()\n        factory = StrategyFactory()\n        self._service = TriplesService(repo=repo, validator=validator, factory=factory, default_strategy=DEFAULT_STRATEGY)\n\n    def call(self, items: List[int], strategy: Optional[str] = None) -> TriplesResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calls the TriplesService to evaluate the given items.\n        It orchestrates the entire process from validation to result.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self._service.evaluate(items, strategy)\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/validators.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nInput validation logic for the application.\nEnsures that input data conforms to expected types and constraints.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Any, List\nfrom .config import MIN_ITEMS\n\nclass ValidationError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input data.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input is a list of integers and meets minimum length.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate(self, items: Any) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates the given items. Raises ValidationError if input is invalid.\n        Checks for list type, minimum length, and integer elements.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(items, list):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input 'items' must be a list.\")\n        if len(items) < MIN_ITEMS:\n            raise ValidationError(f\"Input 'items' must have at least {MIN_ITEMS} elements.\")\n        for i, v in enumerate(items):\n            if not isinstance(v, int):\n                raise ValidationError(f\"Item at index {i} ('{v}') is not an integer.\")\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/utils.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nUtility functions for common tasks like JSON serialization and timestamping.\nThese helpers streamline data manipulation and time management.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom typing import Any\n\nclass DateTimeEncoder(json.JSONEncoder):\n    \"\"\"Custom JSON encoder to handle datetime objects.\"\"\"\n    def default(self, obj: Any) -> Any:\n        if isinstance(obj, datetime):\n            return obj.isoformat()\n        return super().default(obj)\n\ndef to_json(obj: Any) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts a Python object to its JSON string representation.\"\"\"\n    return json.dumps(obj, cls=DateTimeEncoder)\n\ndef from_json(s: str) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Parses a JSON string into a Python object.\"\"\"\n    return json.loads(s)\n\ndef now_utc() -> datetime:\n    \"\"\"Returns the current UTC datetime.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc)\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/repository.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nPersistence layer for evaluation requests and results.\nHandles saving and querying data from a local SQLite database.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport os\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .models import TriplesRequest, TriplesResult\nfrom .utils import to_json, now_utc, from_json\nfrom .config import DB_PATH, DB_DIR\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass TriplesRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistent storage of evaluation requests and results in SQLite.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = DB_PATH) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the repository with the database file path.\"\"\"\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n        os.makedirs(DB_DIR, exist_ok=True) # Ensure data directory exists\n\n    def _connect(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Establishes a connection to the SQLite database, creating it if it doesn't exist.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            _logger.info(f\"Connecting to SQLite database: {self.db_path}\")\n            self._conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path, check_same_thread=False)\n            self._conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;\") # Enable WAL mode for better concurrency\n        return self._conn\n\n    def ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures that the necessary database tables and indexes exist.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._connect()\n        conn.executescript(\"\"\"\n            CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS evaluations (\n              id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n              items TEXT NOT NULL,\n              result INTEGER NOT NULL,\n              strategy TEXT NOT NULL,\n              created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n            );\n            CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_evaluations_created_at ON evaluations(created_at);\n        \"\"\")\n        conn.commit()\n        _logger.info(\"Database schema ensured.\")\n\n    def save_evaluation(self, req: TriplesRequest, res: TriplesResult) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Saves an evaluation request and its result to the database.\n        Returns the ID of the newly inserted row.\n        \"\"\"\n        conn = self._connect()\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        try:\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"INSERT INTO evaluations (items, result, strategy, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                (to_json(req.items), int(res.result), res.strategy, res.timestamp.isoformat()),\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n            _logger.debug(f\"Evaluation saved with ID: {cursor.lastrowid}\")\n            return cursor.lastrowid\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            _logger.error(f\"Failed to save evaluation to DB: {e}\")\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Database error during save: {e}\") from e\n\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Queries and returns a list of recent evaluation records.\n        Returns a list of dictionaries, each representing a row.\n        \"\"\"\n        conn = self._connect()\n        conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row # Return rows as dict-like objects\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        try:\n            cursor.execute(\n                \"SELECT id, items, result, strategy, created_at FROM evaluations ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\",\n                (limit,)\n            )\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            results = []\n            for row in rows:\n                row_dict = dict(row)\n                row_dict['items'] = from_json(row_dict['items']) # Parse JSON back to list\n                row_dict['result'] = bool(row_dict['result']) # Convert int to bool\n                results.append(row_dict)\n            _logger.debug(f\"Queried {len(results)} recent evaluations.\")\n            return results\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            _logger.error(f\"Failed to query recent evaluations: {e}\")\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Database error during query: {e}\") from e\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/algorithms/base.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nBase interface for triplet-sum algorithms.\nAll concrete algorithm strategies must implement this interface.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass IStrategy(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract base class defining the interface for a triplet-sum algorithm.\"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def find_triplet(self, items: List[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if there are three distinct elements in the list that sum to zero.\n        Must be implemented by concrete strategy classes.\n        \"\"\"\n        pass\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/algorithms/brute_force.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nBrute-force algorithm to find three distinct elements that sum to zero.\nThis strategy has a time complexity of O(n^3).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .base import IStrategy\n\nclass BruteForceStrategy(IStrategy):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the brute-force approach to find a zero-sum triplet.\n    It checks all possible combinations of three distinct elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_triplet(self, items: List[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates through all unique combinations of three indices (i, j, k)\n        and checks if their corresponding values sum to zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        n = len(items)\n        # Iterate through all distinct indices i, j, k\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n): # j must be greater than i for distinct indices\n                for k in range(j + 1, n): # k must be greater than j for distinct indices\n                    if items[i] + items[j] + items[k] == 0:\n                        return True\n        return False\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/algorithms/two_pointer.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nOptimized algorithm using sorting and the two-pointer technique.\nThis strategy achieves a time complexity of O(n^2).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .base import IStrategy\n\nclass TwoPointerStrategy(IStrategy):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the two-pointer approach to find a zero-sum triplet.\n    It sorts the array and uses two pointers for efficient searching.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_triplet(self, items: List[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Sorts the input list, then iterates through each element.\n        For each element, it uses two pointers to find two other elements that sum to zero.\n        \"\"\"\n        arr = sorted(items) # Sorting is O(n log n)\n        n = len(arr)\n\n        for i in range(n - 2): # Iterate up to n-3 to ensure at least two elements remain\n            # Initialize two pointers for the rest of the array\n            left, right = i + 1, n - 1\n            while left < right:\n                current_sum = arr[i] + arr[left] + arr[right]\n                if current_sum == 0:\n                    return True # Triplet found\n                elif current_sum < 0:\n                    left += 1 # Move left pointer to increase sum\n                else:\n                    right -= 1 # Move right pointer to decrease sum\n        return False # No triplet found\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/algorithms/factory.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nFactory for creating algorithm strategy instances.\nThis module provides a way to select and instantiate algorithms at runtime.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom .base import IStrategy\nfrom .brute_force import BruteForceStrategy\nfrom .two_pointer import TwoPointerStrategy\n\nclass StrategyFactory:\n    \"\"\"\n    A factory class for retrieving different triplet-sum strategy implementations.\n    It maps strategy names to their respective instances.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the factory with available strategies.\"\"\"\n        self._strategies = {\n            \"brute_force\": BruteForceStrategy(),\n            \"two_pointer\": TwoPointerStrategy(),\n        }\n\n    def get(self, strategy_name: Optional[str]) -> IStrategy:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns an instance of the specified strategy.\n        Raises ValueError if the strategy name is unknown.\n        \"\"\"\n        if strategy_name is None:\n            # Fallback to default if None is provided, handled by service layer\n            raise ValueError(\"Strategy name cannot be None at factory level.\")\n        strategy = self._strategies.get(strategy_name)\n        if not strategy:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Unknown strategy: {strategy_name}. Available strategies: {list(self._strategies.keys())}\")\n        return strategy\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/services.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nService layer that orchestrates validation, algorithm execution, and persistence.\nThis is the core business logic component, coordinating interactions between other layers.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .models import TriplesRequest, TriplesResult\nfrom .repository import TriplesRepository\nfrom .validators import InputValidator, ValidationError\nfrom .algorithms.factory import StrategyFactory\nfrom .algorithms.base import IStrategy\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_STRATEGY\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nclass TriplesService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Orchestrates the process of evaluating a list of integers for a zero-sum triplet.\n    Handles validation, strategy selection, execution, and persistence of results.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        repo: TriplesRepository,\n        validator: InputValidator,\n        factory: StrategyFactory,\n        default_strategy: str = DEFAULT_STRATEGY\n    ) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the service with its dependencies.\"\"\"\n        self.repo = repo\n        self.validator = validator\n        self.factory = factory\n        self.default_strategy = default_strategy\n        self.repo.ensure_schema() # Ensure DB schema is ready when service starts\n\n    def evaluate(self, items: List[int], strategy_name: Optional[str] = None) -> TriplesResult:\n        \"\"\"\n        Evaluates if a zero-sum triplet exists in the given list using a specified strategy.\n        It performs validation, executes the chosen algorithm, and persists the outcome.\n        \"\"\"\n        # 1. Validate input\n        self.validator.validate(items)\n        req = TriplesRequest(items=items)\n\n        # 2. Get strategy\n        chosen_strategy_name = strategy_name if strategy_name else self.default_strategy\n        strategy: IStrategy = self.factory.get(chosen_strategy_name)\n        \n        result_bool: bool = False\n        error_msg: Optional[str] = None\n\n        try:\n            # 3. Execute strategy\n            result_bool = strategy.find_triplet(items)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            _logger.exception(f\"Algorithm {type(strategy).__name__} failed for items: {items}\")\n            error_msg = f\"Algorithm error: {str(exc)}\"\n\n        # 4. Construct result DTO\n        res = TriplesResult(\n            result=result_bool,\n            strategy=type(strategy).__name__,\n            error=error_msg\n        )\n\n        # 5. Persist result (non-fatal)\n        try:\n            self.repo.save_evaluation(req, res)\n        except Exception:\n            _logger.exception(\"Failed to persist evaluation result. Continuing without persistence.\")\n        \n        return res\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/controllers.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nControllers layer handling CLI and REST API interfaces.\nThis module translates external requests into service calls and formats responses.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nimport uvicorn\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, Depends, status\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\nfrom .models import TriplesRequest, TriplesResult\nfrom .services import TriplesService\nfrom .repository import TriplesRepository\nfrom .validators import InputValidator, ValidationError\nfrom .algorithms.factory import StrategyFactory\nfrom .config import DB_PATH, DEFAULT_STRATEGY, LOG_LEVEL\nfrom .utils import to_json\n\n# Configure logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=LOG_LEVEL, stream=sys.stdout, format='%(asctime)s - %(name)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s')\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# --- FastAPI API Controller ---\n\nclass EvaluateRequest(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the API request payload.\"\"\"\n    items: List[int] = Field(..., description=\"A list of integers to evaluate.\")\n    strategy: Optional[str] = Field(None, description=\"Optional algorithm strategy (e.g., 'two_pointer', 'brute_force').\")\n\n# Dependency providers for FastAPI\ndef get_repository() -> TriplesRepository:\n    \"\"\"Provides a TriplesRepository instance.\"\"\"\n    return TriplesRepository(db_path=DB_PATH)\n\ndef get_validator() -> InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Provides an InputValidator instance.\"\"\"\n    return InputValidator()\n\ndef get_strategy_factory() -> StrategyFactory:\n    \"\"\"Provides a StrategyFactory instance.\"\"\"\n    return StrategyFactory()\n\ndef get_triples_service(\n    repo: TriplesRepository = Depends(get_repository),\n    validator: InputValidator = Depends(get_validator),\n    factory: StrategyFactory = Depends(get_strategy_factory),\n) -> TriplesService:\n    \"\"\"Provides a TriplesService instance with its dependencies injected.\"\"\"\n    return TriplesService(repo=repo, validator=validator, factory=factory, default_strategy=DEFAULT_STRATEGY)\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Manages the FastAPI application and its routes.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the FastAPI app and sets up routes.\"\"\"\n        self.app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"Triples Sum to Zero API\",\n            description=\"API service to determine if a list of integers contains three distinct elements that sum to zero.\",\n            version=\"1.0.0\",\n        )\n        self._add_routes()\n\n    def _add_routes(self):\n        \"\"\"Defines the API endpoints.\"\"\"\n        @self.app.post(\"/api/v1/evaluate\", response_model=TriplesResult, status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def post_evaluate(\n            request: EvaluateRequest,\n            service: TriplesService = Depends(get_triples_service)\n        ):\n            \"\"\"\n            Evaluates a list of integers to find if any three distinct elements sum to zero.\n            Returns the result, strategy used, and any errors.\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                # Pydantic handles basic type validation; InputValidator adds length/specific checks.\n                # Re-validate with our custom validator for consistency across interfaces.\n                service.validator.validate(request.items)\n                result = service.evaluate(request.items, request.strategy)\n                return result\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                _logger.warning(f\"API validation error: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=f\"Validation failed: {e}\")\n            except ValueError as e: # Catch ValueErrors from StrategyFactory for unknown strategy\n                _logger.warning(f\"API input error: {e}\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=f\"Bad request: {e}\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                _logger.exception(\"Unexpected error during API evaluation.\")\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n\napi_controller = APIController()\napp = api_controller.app # The FastAPI instance to be run by uvicorn\n\n\n# --- CLI Controller ---\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Manages the command-line interface for evaluating lists.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: TriplesService):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the CLI controller with a TriplesService instance.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Parses command-line arguments and performs the evaluation.\n        Returns an exit code (0 for success, non-zero for errors).\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Determine if a list of integers contains three distinct elements that sum to zero.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.ArgumentDefaultsHelpFormatter\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--items\",\n            type=str,\n            required=True,\n            help=\"JSON string representing a list of integers, e.g., '[1, -1, 0, 0]'\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--strategy\",\n            type=str,\n            default=DEFAULT_STRATEGY,\n            choices=[\"two_pointer\", \"brute_force\"],\n            help=\"Algorithm strategy to use.\"\n        )\n\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\n        try:\n            items_list = json.loads(args.items)\n            result = self.service.evaluate(items_list, args.strategy)\n            print(to_json(result))\n            return 0 # Success\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            _logger.error(f\"CLI input error: Invalid JSON string for --items: '{args.items}'\")\n            print(f\"Error: Invalid JSON string for --items: '{args.items}'\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Validation error / invalid input\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            _logger.error(f\"CLI validation error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: Validation failed: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Validation error\n        except ValueError as e: # Catch ValueError from StrategyFactory for unknown strategy\n            _logger.error(f\"CLI configuration error: {e}\")\n            print(f\"Error: Configuration error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Invalid input/config\n        except Exception as e:\n            _logger.exception(\"Unexpected error during CLI evaluation.\")\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Runtime error\n\ndef main_cli():\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the CLI application.\"\"\"\n    repo = TriplesRepository(db_path=DB_PATH)\n    validator = InputValidator()\n    factory = StrategyFactory()\n    service = TriplesService(repo=repo, validator=validator, factory=factory, default_strategy=DEFAULT_STRATEGY)\n    cli_controller = CLIController(service)\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run(sys.argv))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main_cli() # This allows running `python -m triples_sum.controllers` for CLI\n    # For API, uvicorn must be used: `uvicorn triples_sum.controllers:app --reload`\n```\n\n```\nsrc/triples_sum/algorithms/__init__.py\n```python\n\"\"\"\nAlgorithm package initialization.\nExposes key strategy components for easier import.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .factory import StrategyFactory\nfrom .base import IStrategy\nfrom .brute_force import BruteForceStrategy\nfrom .two_pointer import TwoPointerStrategy\n```\n\n```\nmigrations/001_create_evaluations_table.sql\n```sql\n-- Migration file: 001_create_evaluations_table.sql\n-- This script creates the 'evaluations' table and an index.\n\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS evaluations (\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n  items TEXT NOT NULL,          -- Stores the input list of integers as a JSON string.\n  result INTEGER NOT NULL,      -- Stores the boolean result (0 for False, 1 for True).\n  strategy TEXT NOT NULL,       -- Stores the name of the algorithm strategy used.\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL      -- Stores the UTC timestamp of the evaluation in ISO8601 format.\n);\n\n-- Creates an index on the 'created_at' column to optimize queries\n-- for recent evaluations, often ordered by timestamp.\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_evaluations_created_at ON evaluations(created_at);\n```\n\n```\npyproject.toml\n```toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"triples-sum\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Python library and service to find three distinct elements summing to zero.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"triples_sum\", from=\"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.10\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.4\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\ntriples-sum-cli = \"triples_sum.controllers:main_cli\"\n```\n\n```\nREADME.md\n```markdown\n# Triples Sum to Zero Service\n\nThis project provides a Python library and a small service to determine whether a list of integers contains three distinct elements that sum to zero. It supports multiple algorithm strategies, offers both a CLI and a REST API, and records requests and results persistently for auditing.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Reusable Library**: Core logic encapsulated in a Python library.\n- **Multiple Algorithms**: Supports naive (O(n^3)) and optimized (O(n^2)) algorithms, selectable at runtime.\n- **CLI Interface**: Evaluate lists directly from the command line.\n- **REST API**: Exposes an HTTP endpoint for easy integration.\n- **Persistence**: Records all evaluations to a local SQLite database.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone <repository_url>\ncd triples-sum\n\n# Install dependencies using Poetry\npoetry install\n\n# Activate the poetry shell\npoetry shell\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nTo evaluate a list using the CLI:\n\n```bash\npoetry run triples-sum-cli --items '[1, 3, -2, 1]'\n# Expected output: {\"result\": true, \"strategy\": \"TwoPointerStrategy\", \"error\": null, \"timestamp\": \"...\"}\n\npoetry run triples-sum-cli --items '[-5, 2, 3, 9, 7, 4]' --strategy brute_force\n# Expected output: {\"result\": true, \"strategy\": \"BruteForceStrategy\", \"error\": null, \"timestamp\": \"...\"}\n\npoetry run triples-sum-cli --items '[1, 2]'\n# Expected output: Error: Validation failed: Input 'items' must have at least 3 elements.\n```\n\n### REST API\n\nTo start the REST API server (requires `uvicorn` installed, which is included in `poetry install`):\n\n```bash\npoetry run uvicorn triples_sum.controllers:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\nThe API will be available at `http://0.0.0.0:8000`. You can send POST requests to `/api/v1/evaluate`.\n\n**Example Request (using `curl`):**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"http://localhost:8000/api/v1/evaluate\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\n           \"items\": [1, 3, -2, 1],\n           \"strategy\": \"two_pointer\"\n         }'\n```\n\n**Example Response (200 OK):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": true,\n  \"strategy\": \"TwoPointerStrategy\",\n  \"error\": null,\n  \"timestamp\": \"2023-10-27T10:30:00.123456\"\n}\n```\n\n**Example Response (400 Bad Request for validation error):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": \"Validation failed: Input 'items' must have at least 3 elements.\"\n}\n```\n\n### Database Inspection\n\nThe evaluations are stored in a SQLite database at `./data/triples_sum.db`. You can use a SQLite client to inspect the `evaluations` table:\n\n```bash\nsqlite3 data/triples_sum.db \"SELECT * FROM evaluations;\"\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 triples_sum/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 models.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 external.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validators.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 repository.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controllers.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 algorithms/\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 base.py\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 brute_force.py\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 two_pointer.py\n\u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500 factory.py\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 migrations/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 001_create_evaluations_table.sql\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 LICENSE\n```\n\n## Development\n\nThe project uses `poetry` for dependency management.\n\n```bash\n# Run linters\npoetry run flake8 src/\n\n# (Unit tests are not included in this generation as per requirements,\n# but would typically be run with `poetry run pytest`)\n```\n```\n\n```\nLICENSE\n```\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) [Year] [Your Name]\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\no