{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def encode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns encoded string by shifting every character by 5 in the alphabet.\n    This implementation assumes input consists only of lowercase letters a-z.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([chr(((ord(ch) + 5 - ord(\"a\")) % 26) + ord(\"a\")) for ch in s])\n\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes as input string encoded with encode_shift function. Returns decoded string.\n    This implementation assumes input consists only of lowercase letters a-z.\n    \"\"\"\n    return \"\".join([chr(((ord(ch) - 5 - ord(\"a\")) % 26) + ord(\"a\")) for ch in s])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def encode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns encoded string by shifting every lowercase ASCII character by 5 in the alphabet.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are preserved as they are.\n    \"\"\"\n    res = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            res.append(chr(((ord(ch) + 5 - ord('a')) % 26) + ord('a')))\n        else:\n            res.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(res)\n\n\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string encoded with encode_shift by shifting every lowercase ASCII character by -5.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are preserved as they are.\n    \"\"\"\n    res = []\n    for ch in s:\n        if 'a' <= ch <= 'z':\n            res.append(chr(((ord(ch) - 5 - ord('a')) % 26) + ord('a')))\n        else:\n            res.append(ch)\n    return \"\".join(res)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "def remove_vowels(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes all occurrences of vowels (a, e, i, o, u and their uppercase variants) from the input string.\n    Preserves all other characters including spaces, punctuation, and newlines.\n    \"\"\"\n    VOWELS = frozenset({'a','e','i','o','u','A','E','I','O','U'})\n    result = ''.join(ch for ch in text if ch not in VOWELS)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/51", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_vowels(text):\n    \"\"\"\n    remove_vowels is a function that takes string and returns string without vowels.\n    Vowels (a, e, i, o, u) are removed case-insensitively while preserving other characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    vowel_set = frozenset(\"aeiou\")\n    return ''.join(char for char in text if char.lower() not in vowel_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/52", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"numutils\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small Python library to check if all numeric values in a list are below a given threshold.\"\nauthors = [{ name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" }]\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\ndependencies = [\n    \"Flask>=2.0.0\", # For the optional HTTP API\n]\n\n[project.readme]\nfile = \"README.md\"\ncontent-type = \"text/markdown\"\n\n[project.scripts]\nnumutils = \"numutils.cli:main\" # CLI entry point\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0.0\",\n    \"pytest-cov>=4.0.0\",\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0.0\"] # Or \"poetry-core>=1.0.0\" if using Poetry\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\" # Or \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n# README.md\n# numutils\nA small, well-tested Python library to determine if all numeric values in a list are below a given threshold.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Library API**: `numutils.below_threshold(l: list, t: int)`\n- **CLI**: `numutils below-threshold --values \"1,2,3\" --threshold 5`\n- **HTTP Endpoint**: A lightweight Flask server exposes `POST /v1/below-threshold`\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install numutils\n```\n\nFor the optional HTTP API server, you'll need Flask:\n```bash\npip install \"numutils[api]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom numutils import below_threshold\nfrom numutils.exceptions import ValidationError\n\n# All values below threshold\nprint(below_threshold([1, 5, 9], 10))  # Output: True\n\n# Some value at or above threshold\nprint(below_threshold([1, 5, 10], 10)) # Output: False\n\n# Empty list (vacuously true)\nprint(below_threshold([], 10))      # Output: True\n\n# Invalid inputs raise ValidationError\ntry:\n    below_threshold([1, 'a', 3], 5)\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Output: Error: value at index 1 is not numeric: 'a'\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\n# Basic usage\nnumutils below-threshold --values \"1,2,3\" --threshold 5\n# Output: True\n\nnumutils below-threshold --values \"1,2,5\" --threshold 5\n# Output: False\n\n# Empty list\nnumutils below-threshold --values \"\" --threshold 0\n# Output: True\n\n# Invalid input\nnumutils below-threshold --values \"1,a,3\" --threshold 5\n# Output: Error: value at index 1 is not numeric: 'a' (exit code 2)\n```\n\n### HTTP Endpoint\n\nTo run the server (requires Flask):\n```bash\npython -m numutils.api\n```\nBy default, it runs on `http://127.0.0.1:5000`.\n\nThen, you can use `curl` or any HTTP client:\n```bash\n# Example success\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"values\":[1,2,3], \"threshold\":5}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1/below-threshold\n# Output: {\"below\":true}\n\n# Example failure\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"values\":[1,2,5], \"threshold\":5}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1/below-threshold\n# Output: {\"below\":false}\n\n# Example validation error\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"values\":[1,\"a\",3], \"threshold\":5}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1/below-threshold\n# Output: {\"error\":\"value at index 1 is not numeric: 'a'\"} (HTTP 400)\n```\n\n---\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/__init__.py\n\"\"\"\nnumutils - A library for numeric list utilities.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .services import BelowThresholdService\nfrom .validators import ThresholdValidator\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError, NumUtilsError\nfrom .client import Client\n\n# Initialize a default client for direct library calls\n_default_client = Client(service=BelowThresholdService(validator=ThresholdValidator()))\n\ndef below_threshold(l: list, t: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return True if all numeric values in the list 'l' are strictly below 't'.\n\n    Args:\n        l: An iterable of numbers (int or float).\n        t: A numeric threshold (int or float).\n\n    Returns:\n        True if every numeric element x in l satisfies x < t; otherwise False.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValidationError: If 'l' is not iterable, contains non-numeric elements,\n                         or 't' is not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _default_client.is_below(l, t)\n\n# Re-export key components for explicit access if needed\n__all__ = [\n    \"below_threshold\",\n    \"BelowThresholdService\",\n    \"ThresholdValidator\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n    \"NumUtilsError\",\n    \"Client\",\n]\n\n# For CLI entry point\nfrom . import cli\ndef main():\n    cli.main()\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/services.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .validators import ThresholdValidator\n\nclass BelowThresholdService:\n    \"\"\"\n    Core business logic for determining if all numbers in a list are below a threshold.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, validator: ThresholdValidator):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the service with a validator.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def below_threshold(self, values: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates inputs and returns True if each element x satisfies x < threshold.\n        \"\"\"\n        validated_values, validated_threshold = self._validator.validate_values(values, threshold)\n        return self._all_below(validated_values, validated_threshold)\n\n    def _all_below(self, values: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Efficient O(n) loop, returning False early if any element >= threshold.\n        \"\"\"\n        for x in values:\n            if x >= threshold:\n                return False\n        return True\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/validators.py\nfrom typing import Iterable, Tuple, Any\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass ThresholdValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates and normalizes input values and threshold to numeric types (float).\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate_values(self, values: Iterable[Any], threshold: Any) -> Tuple[List[float], float]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Ensures 'values' is iterable and contains only ints/floats; converts to float list.\n        Ensures 'threshold' is numeric and converts to float.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(values, Iterable):\n            raise ValidationError(\"values must be an iterable\")\n\n        out_values = []\n        for idx, v in enumerate(values):\n            if not self._is_number(v):\n                raise ValidationError(f\"value at index {idx} is not numeric: {v!r}\")\n            out_values.append(float(v))\n\n        if not self._is_number(threshold):\n            raise ValidationError(\"threshold must be a numeric type\")\n\n        return out_values, float(threshold)\n\n    def _is_number(self, obj: Any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper method returning True for int/float, excluding bool (as bool is subclass of int).\n        \"\"\"\n        return isinstance(obj, (int, float)) and not isinstance(obj, bool)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/dtos.py\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass BelowThresholdRequest:\n    \"\"\"\n    Data Transfer Object for below_threshold request, used by API.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, values: List[float], threshold: float):\n        self.values = values\n        self.threshold = threshold\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_json(data: Dict[str, Any]) -> \"BelowThresholdRequest\":\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates presence of keys and basic types, produces DTO from JSON dictionary.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            raise ValidationError(\"JSON body must be an object\")\n        if \"values\" not in data:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Key 'values' is required in the request body\")\n        if \"threshold\" not in data:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Key 'threshold' is required in the request body\")\n        \n        values_raw = data[\"values\"]\n        threshold_raw = data[\"threshold\"]\n\n        if not isinstance(values_raw, list):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Field 'values' must be a list\")\n        if not (isinstance(threshold_raw, (int, float)) and not isinstance(threshold_raw, bool)):\n            raise ValidationError(\"Field 'threshold' must be a number\")\n\n        # Basic type checks for list elements - full validation via ThresholdValidator\n        for idx, val in enumerate(values_raw):\n            if not (isinstance(val, (int, float)) and not isinstance(val, bool)):\n                raise ValidationError(f\"Value at index {idx} in 'values' is not numeric: {val!r}\")\n\n        return BelowThresholdRequest(values=values_raw, threshold=float(threshold_raw))\n\nclass BelowThresholdResponse:\n    \"\"\"\n    Data Transfer Object for below_threshold response, used by API.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, below: bool):\n        self.below = below\n\n    def to_json(self) -> Dict[str, bool]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns dictionary representation for JSON serialization.\n        \"\"\"\n        return {\"below\": self.below}\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/exceptions.py\nclass NumUtilsError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for numutils library errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass ValidationError(NumUtilsError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when input validation fails.\"\"\"\n    pass\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/cli.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\nfrom .services import BelowThresholdService\nfrom .validators import ThresholdValidator\nfrom .utils import parse_values_arg\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    CLI parsing and orchestration for the numutils commands.\n    \"\"\"\n    def run_cli(self, argv: List[str], service: Optional[BelowThresholdService] = None) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Entrypoint for console_scripts; parses args, calls service, prints result.\n        Returns an exit code: 0 for success, 2 for validation error, 1 for other errors.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = self._build_parser()\n        args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n        # Default service if not provided (for dependency injection / testing)\n        svc = service or BelowThresholdService(ThresholdValidator())\n\n        try:\n            # parse_values_arg handles empty string for --values\n            values = parse_values_arg(args.values or \"\")\n            # threshold will be validated by the service/validator, but argparse gives us a string\n            threshold = float(args.threshold) \n            \n            result = svc.below_threshold(values, threshold)\n            print(\"True\" if result else \"False\")\n            return 0\n        except ValidationError as ve:\n            print(f\"Error: {ve}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except ValueError as ve: # Catch float conversion errors from argparse\n            print(f\"Error parsing arguments: {ve}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n    def _build_parser(self) -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n        \"\"\"\n        Builds the argparse parser for the below-threshold command.\n        \"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"numutils below-threshold\",\n            description=\"Check if all numeric values in a list are below a threshold.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--values\",\n            type=str,\n            default=\"\",\n            help=\"Comma-separated list of numbers (e.g., '1,2.5,3'). Defaults to empty list.\",\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"--threshold\",\n            type=float, # Argparse can handle initial float conversion\n            required=True,\n            help=\"The numeric threshold.\"\n        )\n        return parser\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI.\"\"\"\n    controller = CLIController()\n    sys.exit(controller.run_cli(sys.argv[1:]))\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/api.py\nfrom flask import Flask, request, jsonify\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom .services import BelowThresholdService\nfrom .validators import ThresholdValidator\nfrom .dtos import BelowThresholdRequest, BelowThresholdResponse\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"\n    Provides a Flask application factory exposing the /v1/below-threshold endpoint.\n    \"\"\"\n    def create_app(self, service: Optional[BelowThresholdService] = None) -> Flask:\n        \"\"\"\n        Creates and returns a Flask app instance.\n        If no service is provided, a default service with a ThresholdValidator is used.\n        \"\"\"\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n        # Initialize service with default validator if not provided (for testing/DI)\n        svc = service or BelowThresholdService(validator=ThresholdValidator())\n\n        @app.route(\"/v1/below-threshold\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n        def below_threshold_endpoint():\n            \"\"\"\n            Handles POST requests to /v1/below-threshold.\n            Accepts JSON {\"values\":[...],\"threshold\":...} and returns {\"below\":true/false}.\n            \"\"\"\n            try:\n                # Flask's get_json() handles Content-Type check and parsing\n                data = request.get_json(force=True) # force=True allows non-application/json, but might mask client errors\n                \n                # Use DTO for initial structure validation\n                dto = BelowThresholdRequest.from_json(data)\n                \n                # Delegate to the core service logic\n                result = svc.below_threshold(dto.values, dto.threshold)\n                \n                # Return success response\n                return jsonify(BelowThresholdResponse(below=result).to_json()), 200\n            except ValidationError as ve:\n                # Handle specific validation errors from DTO or service\n                return jsonify({\"error\": str(ve)}), 400\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch any unexpected errors and return a generic 500\n                app.logger.error(f\"Internal server error: {e}\", exc_info=True)\n                return jsonify({\"error\": \"internal server error\"}), 500\n\n        # Register error handlers (e.g., for JSON parsing errors before route is hit)\n        @app.errorhandler(400) # Bad Request generally covers JSON parsing issues\n        def handle_bad_request(error):\n            if request.is_json:\n                try:\n                    request.get_json() # Try parsing again to get specific error message\n                except Exception as e:\n                    return jsonify({\"error\": f\"Invalid JSON payload: {e}\"}), 400\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Bad request\"}), 400\n\n        return app\n\n# Main entry point for running the Flask app directly (e.g., `python -m numutils.api`)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    api_controller = APIController()\n    app = api_controller.create_app()\n    app.run(debug=True, host=\"0.0.0.0\") # Consider disabling debug in production\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/client.py\nfrom typing import Iterable, Optional\n\nfrom .services import BelowThresholdService\nfrom .validators import ThresholdValidator\n\nclass Client:\n    \"\"\"\n    A programmatic wrapper around the BelowThresholdService for ease of use.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: Optional[BelowThresholdService] = None):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes the client, optionally with a custom service.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._service = service or BelowThresholdService(validator=ThresholdValidator())\n\n    def is_below(self, values: Iterable, threshold: float) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if all numeric values in the given iterable are strictly below the threshold.\n        Delegates to the internal BelowThresholdService.\n        \"\"\"\n        # The service's below_threshold method expects list[float] and float\n        # but the validator handles conversion from Iterable and object\n        return self._service.below_threshold(values, threshold)\n```\n\n```python\n# src/numutils/utils.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import ValidationError\n\ndef parse_number(s: str) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a string to a float. Raises ValidationError on failure.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        return float(s)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValidationError(f\"Cannot parse '{s}' as a number\")\n\ndef parse_values_arg(s: str) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Parses a comma-separated string of numbers into a list of floats.\n    Handles empty string by returning an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return []\n    \n    parts = s.split(',')\n    parsed_numbers = []\n    for part in parts:\n        stripped_part = part.strip()\n        if not stripped_part: # Handle empty parts like \"1,,3\"\n            raise ValidationError(\"Empty string found between commas in values argument\")\n        parsed_numbers.append(parse_number(stripped_part))\n    return parsed_numbers\n```"}
