.\n- **CLI Tool**: `will-it-fly` to check conditions from the command line.\n- **HTTP API**: `POST /api/v1/will_it_fly` for integration with other systems.\n- Input validation, clear error messages, and structured responses.\n\n## Installation\n\n### Using Poetry (recommended)\n\n1.  Clone the repository:\n    `git clone https://github.com/your-org/will-it-fly.git`\n    `cd will-it-fly`\n2.  Install dependencies:\n    `poetry install`\n3.  If you want to run the HTTP server, install with the `http` extra:\n    `poetry install --extras http`\n\n### Using pip\n\n1.  Clone the repository and navigate into it.\n2.  Install dependencies:\n    `pip install -r requirements.txt`\n    `pip install .` (to install the package itself)\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library Function\n\n```python\nfrom will_it_fly import will_it_fly\n\n# Balanced and within weight\nresult, reason = will_it_fly([3, 2, 3], 9)\nprint(f\"Will it fly? {result}, Reason: {reason}\") # True, '8 <= 9'\n\n# Unbalanced\nresult, reason = will_it_fly([1, 2], 5)\nprint(f\"Will it fly? {result}, Reason: {reason}\") # False, 'unbalanced'\n\n# Too heavy\nresult, reason = will_it_fly([3, 2, 3], 1)\nprint(f\"Will it fly? {result}, Reason: {reason}\") # False, 'too heavy: 8 > 1'\n\n# Invalid input\ntry:\n    will_it_fly([1, \"a\"], 5)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e}\") # Error: Invalid payload: all elements of q must be integers\n```\n\n### CLI Tool\n\nThe CLI tool can accept input via JSON or positional arguments.\n\n**JSON Input:**\n```bash\npoetry run will-it-fly -j '{\"q\": [3, 2, 3], \"w\": 9}'\n# Output: Will fly: True. Reason: 8 <= 9\n\npoetry run will-it-fly -j '{\"q\": [1, 2], \"w\": 5}'\n# Output: Will fly: False. Reason: unbalanced\n\npoetry run will-it-fly -j '{\"q\": [3, 2, 3], \"w\": 1}'\n# Output: Will fly: False. Reason: too heavy: 8 > 1\n\npoetry run will-it-fly -j '{\"q\": [1, \"a\"], \"w\": 5}'\n# Output: Invalid input: all elements of q must be integers\n# Exit code: 2\n```\n\n**Positional Arguments:**\n(q is a comma-separated list of integers, w is an integer)\n```bash\npoetry run will-it-fly \"3,2,3\" 9\n# Output: Will fly: True. Reason: 8 <= 9\n\npoetry run will-it-fly \"1,2\" 5\n# Output: Will fly: False. Reason: unbalanced\n\npoetry run will-it-fly \"3,2,3\" 1\n# Output: Will fly: False. Reason: too heavy: 8 > 1\n\npoetry run will-it-fly \"1,a\" 5\n# Output: Invalid input: q must be a comma-separated list of integers. 'a' is not a valid integer.\n# Exit code: 2\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nFirst, ensure you have installed with `poetry install --extras http` or `pip install fastapi uvicorn`.\n\nTo start the server:\n```bash\nuvicorn will_it_fly.app:AppFactory().create_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\nThen, you can send POST requests:\n\n**Request (JSON):**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"q\": [3, 2, 3], \"w\": 9}' http://localhost:8000/api/v1/will_it_fly\n```\n**Response (200 OK):**\n```json\n{\"will_fly\": true, \"reason\": \"8 <= 9\"}\n```\n\n**Request (Invalid Payload):**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"q\": [1, \"a\"], \"w\": 5}' http://localhost:8000/api/v1/will_it_fly\n```\n**Response (400 Bad Request):**\n```json\n{\"detail\": \"all elements of q must be integers\"}\n```\n\n## Development and Testing\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\nor\n```bash\npytest\n```\n\n### Code Formatting\n\nThis project uses `black` for code formatting.\n```bash\npoetry run black .\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 requirements.txt\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 .github/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 will_it_fly/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __main__.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 app.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 payload.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 exceptions.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 utils/\n\u2502       \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 input_parser.py\n\u2502       \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 console_adapter.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validators/\n\u2502       \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 palindrome_validator.py\n\u2502       \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 weight_validator.py\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 services/\n\u2502       \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502       \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 flight_service.py\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 controllers/\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py\n\u2502           \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli_controller.py\n\u2502           \u2514\u2500\u2500 http_controller.py\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 tests/\n    \u251c\u2500\u2500 unit/\n    \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_palindrome_validator.py\n    \u2502   \u251c\u2500\u2500 test_weight_validator.py\n    \u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_flight_service.py\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 integration/\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 test_http_controller.py\n```\n\n## Contributing\n\nFeel free to open issues or submit pull requests.\n\n## License\n\nThis project is licensed under the MIT License.\n\n```\n```\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [ main ]\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [ main ]\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    strategy:\n      matrix:\n        python-version: [\"3.9\", \"3.10\", \"3.11\", \"3.12\"]\n\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n    - name: Set up Python ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: ${{ matrix.python-version }}\n        cache: 'poetry'\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n    - name: Configure Poetry virtualenvs\n      run: poetry config virtualenvs.in-project true\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root --with dev,http\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: poetry run pytest\n    - name: Check code style with Black\n      run: poetry run black --check .\n    - name: Lint with flake8\n      run: poetry run flake8 .\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/exceptions.py\nclass InvalidPayloadError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input payload.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/payload.py\nfrom typing import List, Any\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidPayloadError\n\nclass Payload:\n    \"\"\"Represents the input payload for the flight check.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, q: List[int], w: int) -> None:\n        self.q = q\n        self.w = w\n\n    def validate(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates the payload ensuring correct types and ranges.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(self.q, list):\n            raise InvalidPayloadError(\"q must be a list of integers\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in self.q):\n            raise InvalidPayloadError(\"all elements of q must be integers\")\n        if not isinstance(self.w, int):\n            raise InvalidPayloadError(\"w must be an integer\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/utils/input_parser.py\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Union\nfrom ..payload import Payload\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidPayloadError\n\nclass InputParser:\n    \"\"\"Handles parsing various input formats into a Payload object.\"\"\"\n    DEFAULT_Q_DELIMITER: str = ','\n\n    def parse_q_string(self, qs: str) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Parses a comma-separated string into a list of integers.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            return [int(x.strip()) for x in qs.split(self.DEFAULT_Q_DELIMITER)]\n        except ValueError as e:\n            raise InvalidPayloadError(\n                f\"q must be a comma-separated list of integers. Part of it is not valid: {e}\"\n            )\n\n    def parse_cli_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> Payload:\n        \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments to construct a Payload.\"\"\"\n        if \"-j\" in argv:\n            try:\n                json_index = argv.index(\"-j\")\n                json_str = argv[json_index + 1]\n                data: Dict[str, Union[List[int], int]] = json.loads(json_str)\n                return Payload(data.get(\"q\"), data.get(\"w\"))\n            except (IndexError, json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError, ValueError) as e:\n                raise InvalidPayloadError(f\"Invalid JSON input for -j: {e}\")\n        elif len(argv) == 2:\n            try:\n                q = self.parse_q_string(argv[0])\n                w = int(argv[1])\n                return Payload(q, w)\n            except ValueError as e:\n                raise InvalidPayloadError(f\"Invalid integer for w: {e}\")\n        else:\n            raise InvalidPayloadError(\n                \"Invalid arguments. Use -j '{\\\"q\\\":[1,2],\\\"w\\\":5}' or '1,2' 5\"\n            )\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/utils/console_adapter.py\nclass ConsoleAdapter:\n    \"\"\"Provides utilities for console output.\"\"\"\n    def print_result(self, will_fly: bool, reason: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints the flight result and reason to the console.\"\"\"\n        print(f\"Will fly: {will_fly}. Reason: {reason}\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/validators/palindrome_validator.py\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass PalindromeValidator:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list of integers is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n    def is_palindrome(self, q: List[int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if the list q is a palindrome, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n        return q == q[::-1]\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/validators/weight_validator.py\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass WeightValidator:\n    \"\"\"Calculates total weight and checks against a maximum.\"\"\"\n    def total_weight(self, q: List[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the sum of elements in list q.\"\"\"\n        return sum(q)\n\n    def is_within_weight(self, q: List[int], w: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if the total weight of q is less than or equal to w.\"\"\"\n        return self.total_weight(q) <= w\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/services/flight_service.py\nfrom typing import Tuple\nfrom ..payload import Payload\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidPayloadError\nfrom ..validators.palindrome_validator import PalindromeValidator\nfrom ..validators.weight_validator import WeightValidator\n\nclass FlightService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates validation to determine if an object will fly.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, pal_validator: PalindromeValidator, weight_validator: WeightValidator) -> None:\n        self.pal_validator = pal_validator\n        self.weight_validator = weight_validator\n\n    def will_it_fly(self, payload: Payload) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the object described by the payload will fly.\"\"\"\n        payload.validate()  # FR1: Validate input payload\n\n        # FR2: Check if q is balanced (palindromic)\n        if not self.pal_validator.is_palindrome(payload.q):\n            return False, \"unbalanced\"\n\n        # FR3: Compute total weight and compare to maximum\n        total_q_weight = self.weight_validator.total_weight(payload.q)\n        if total_q_weight > payload.w:\n            return False, f\"too heavy: {total_q_weight} > {payload.w}\"\n\n        # FR4: Return True if both conditions met\n        return True, f\"{total_q_weight} <= {payload.w}\"\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/controllers/cli_controller.py\nimport sys\nfrom typing import List\nfrom ..services.flight_service import FlightService\nfrom ..utils.input_parser import InputParser\nfrom ..utils.console_adapter import ConsoleAdapter\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidPayloadError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface interactions.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FlightService, parser: InputParser, console: ConsoleAdapter) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n        self.parser = parser\n        self.console = console\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI logic, parsing args and printing results.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            payload = self.parser.parse_cli_args(argv)\n            will_fly, reason = self.service.will_it_fly(payload)\n            self.console.print_result(will_fly, reason)\n            return 0\n        except InvalidPayloadError as e:\n            print(f\"Invalid input: {e.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/controllers/http_controller.py\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException\nfrom typing import Dict, Any\nfrom ..services.flight_service import FlightService\nfrom ..payload import Payload\nfrom ..exceptions import InvalidPayloadError\n\nclass HTTPController:\n    \"\"\"Manages FastAPI routes for the flight check service.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: FlightService) -> None:\n        self.service = service\n\n    def router(self) -> APIRouter:\n        \"\"\"Returns an APIRouter with the /will_it_fly endpoint.\"\"\"\n        router = APIRouter()\n\n        @router.post(\"/will_it_fly\", summary=\"Check if an object will fly\")\n        def post_will_it_fly(payload_data: Dict[str, Any]):\n            \"\"\"Receives object data and returns whether it will fly.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                p = Payload(payload_data.get(\"q\"), payload_data.get(\"w\"))\n                will_fly, reason = self.service.will_it_fly(p)\n                return {\"will_fly\": will_fly, \"reason\": reason}\n            except InvalidPayloadError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail=e.message)\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch unexpected errors to return a 500\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=f\"Internal server error: {e}\")\n\n        return router\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/app.py\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom .validators.palindrome_validator import PalindromeValidator\nfrom .validators.weight_validator import WeightValidator\nfrom .services.flight_service import FlightService\nfrom .controllers.http_controller import HTTPController\n\nclass AppFactory:\n    \"\"\"Factory to create and configure the FastAPI application.\"\"\"\n    API_PREFIX = \"/api/v1\"\n\n    def create_app(self) -> FastAPI:\n        \"\"\"Initializes and returns a FastAPI application instance.\"\"\"\n        pal_validator = PalindromeValidator()\n        weight_validator = WeightValidator()\n        service = FlightService(pal_validator, weight_validator)\n        http_controller = HTTPController(service)\n\n        app = FastAPI(\n            title=\"WillItFly Service\",\n            description=\"A service to determine if an object will fly based on balance and weight.\",\n            version=\"0.1.0\",\n        )\n        app.include_router(http_controller.router(), prefix=self.API_PREFIX)\n        return app\n\n# This allows uvicorn to directly call `uvicorn will_it_fly.app:AppFactory().create_app --reload`\n# The factory pattern provides more control over dependency injection if needed for testing or different environments.\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/__main__.py\nimport sys\nfrom .validators.palindrome_validator import PalindromeValidator\nfrom .validators.weight_validator import WeightValidator\nfrom .services.flight_service import FlightService\nfrom .utils.input_parser import InputParser\nfrom .utils.console_adapter import ConsoleAdapter\nfrom .controllers.cli_controller import CLIController\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    pal_validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    weight_validator = WeightValidator()\n    flight_service = FlightService(pal_validator, weight_validator)\n    input_parser = InputParser()\n    console_adapter = ConsoleAdapter()\n    cli_controller = CLIController(flight_service, input_parser, console_adapter)\n    sys.exit(cli_controller.run(sys.argv[1:]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n```python\n# src/will_it_fly/__init__.py\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n# Import core components to be wrapped by the public function\nfrom .payload import Payload\nfrom .services.flight_service import FlightService\nfrom .validators.palindrome_validator import PalindromeValidator\nfrom .validators.weight_validator import WeightValidator\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidPayloadError # Re-export for library users\n\n# Public library function as per specification\ndef will_it_fly(q: List[int], w: int) -> Tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an object 'will fly' based on balance (palindromic list)\n    and total weight <= maximum allowed weight.\n\n    Args:\n        q: A list of integers representing the object's components.\n        w: An integer representing the maximum allowed weight.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple (bool, str) indicating whether it will fly and a reason.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidPayloadError: If inputs q or w are not of the expected types.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Instantiate dependencies (simple setup for library function facade)\n    pal_validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    weight_validator = WeightValidator()\n    service = FlightService(pal_validator, weight_validator)\n\n    # Create payload and call the service logic\n    payload = Payload(q, w)\n    return service.will_it_fly(payload)\n\n__all__ = [\"will_it_fly\", \"InvalidPayloadError\"]\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/unit/test_palindrome_validator.py\nfrom will_it_fly.validators.palindrome_validator import PalindromeValidator\n\ndef test_even_length_palindrome():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([1, 2, 2, 1]) is True\n\ndef test_odd_length_palindrome():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]) is True\n\ndef test_non_palindrome():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([1, 2, 3]) is False\n\ndef test_single_element_list():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([5]) is True\n\ndef test_empty_list():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([]) is True\n\ndef test_negative_numbers_palindrome():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([-1, 0, -1]) is True\n\ndef test_zeroes_palindrome():\n    validator = PalindromeValidator()\n    assert validator.is_palindrome([0, 0, 0]) is True\n\n```\n```python\n# tests/unit/test_weight_validator.py\nfrom will_it_fly.validators.weight_validator import WeightValidator\n\ndef test_total_weight_positive_numbers():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.total_weight([1, 2, 3]) == 6\n\ndef test_total_weight_negative_numbers():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.total_weight([-1, -2, 3]) == 0\n\ndef test_total_weight_mixed_numbers():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.total_weight([-1, 0, 1]) == 0\n\ndef test_total_weight_empty_list():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.total_weight([]) == 0\n\ndef test_is_within_weight_true():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([1, 2, 3], 6) is True\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([1, 2, 3], 7) is True\n\ndef test_is_within_weight_false():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([1, 2, 3], 5) is False\n\ndef test_is_within_weight_with_negative_w():\n    validator = WeightValidator()\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([1, 2], -1) is False\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([-1, 0], -1) is False # sum is -1, -1 <= -1 is true\n    assert validator.is_within_weight([-1, 0], -2) is False #