{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "def anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a string by sorting characters within each word by ASCII value.\n    Preserves original word order and blank space positions in the sentence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    tokens = []\n    current_token = \"\"\n    # Determine if the first character is a space to start the correct token type\n    is_current_token_space = s[0] == ' '\n\n    for char in s:\n        # If the current character's type (space/non-space) matches the current token's type\n        if (char == ' ') == is_current_token_space:\n            current_token += char\n        else:\n            # Type has changed, so store the current token and start a new one\n            tokens.append(current_token)\n            current_token = char\n            is_current_token_space = (char == ' ')\n    # Add the last token after the loop finishes\n    tokens.append(current_token)\n\n    transformed_tokens = []\n    for token in tokens:\n        # If the token consists only of spaces, append it as is\n        if token and all(c == ' ' for c in token):\n            transformed_tokens.append(token)\n        else:\n            # Otherwise, sort the characters within the word by their ASCII value\n            transformed_tokens.append(''.join(sorted(token, key=ord)))\n\n    # Join all the transformed tokens back into a single string\n    return ''.join(transformed_tokens)"}
