rom .even_odd_service import EvenOddService\nfrom .validator import Validator\nfrom .controller import Controller\nfrom .cli import CLI\nfrom .api import API\n\n# Initialize core dependencies\n_metrics_repo = MetricsRepository()\n_even_odd_service = EvenOddService()\n_validator = Validator()\n\n# Initialize Controller (DI)\ncontroller = Controller(\n    service=_even_odd_service,\n    validator=_validator,\n    metrics_repo=_metrics_repo\n)\n\n# Initialize CLI (DI)\ncli = CLI(controller=controller)\n\n# Initialize Config (can be loaded from environment variables)\n# Example: export EVEN_AT_ODD_API_KEY=\"your_secret_key\"\n_api_key = os.getenv(\"EVEN_AT_ODD_API_KEY\")\n_host = os.getenv(\"EVEN_AT_ODD_HOST\", Config.DEFAULT_HOST)\n_port = int(os.getenv(\"EVEN_AT_ODD_PORT\", Config.DEFAULT_PORT))\n\nconfig = Config(api_key=_api_key, host=_host, port=_port)\n\n# Initialize API (DI)\n_api_instance = API(controller=controller, config=config)\napp = _api_instance.create_app() # The FastAPI app instance for uvicorn\n\n# Expose key components for direct library use\n__all__ = [\n    \"EvenOddService\",\n    \"Validator\",\n    \"Controller\",\n    \"MetricsRepository\",\n    \"Config\",\n    \"ValidationError\",\n    \"InputDTO\",\n    \"ResultDTO\",\n    \"utils\", # If utils functions are to be exposed directly\n    \"cli\", # The CLI instance for main entrypoint\n    \"app\", # The FastAPI application instance\n    \"API\", # The API class if advanced customization is needed\n]\n\n```\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"even-at-odd\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A service to sum even elements at odd indices in a list of integers.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"even_at_odd\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.30.1\"}\npydantic = \"^2.0\" # Use pydantic for DTOs as it's common with FastAPI\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.0.0\"\nhttpx = \"^0.27.0\" # For API testing\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\neven-at-odd = \"even_at_odd.cli:cli.run\" # Entry point for the CLI\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# Even At Odd Sum Service\n\nThis project provides a reusable Python library, a Command Line Interface (CLI), and an HTTP API to compute the sum of even elements that are located at odd indices within a non-empty list of integers.\n\n## 1. Features\n\n-   **Core Logic**: Efficiently calculates the sum (O(n) time, O(1) additional memory).\n-   **Input Validation**: Robust validation for various input forms.\n-   **Library API**: Direct programmatic access in Python.\n-   **CLI**: Command-line tool for quick calculations.\n-   **HTTP API**: RESTful endpoint for integration.\n-   **Metrics**: In-memory tracking of invocation count and last result.\n-   **Configurable Security**: Optional API key authentication for HTTP API.\n\n## 2. Installation\n\n1.  **Clone the repository:**\n    ```bash\n    git clone https://github.com/yourusername/even-at-odd.git\n    cd even-at-odd\n    ```\n2.  **Install dependencies using Poetry:**\n    ```bash\n    poetry install\n    ```\n    If you don't have Poetry, install it first: `pip install poetry`\n\n## 3. Usage\n\n### 3.1. Library Mode\n\nYou can import the `controller` or `EvenOddService` directly into your Python code.\n\n```python\nfrom even_at_odd.controller import controller\nfrom even_at_odd.validation_error import ValidationError\n\n# Example 1: Basic usage\nnumbers = [4, 2, 6, 7, 8, 9]\ntry:\n    result = controller.compute(numbers)\n    print(f\"Result for {numbers}: {result}\") # Expected: 2 (from index 1)\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e.message}\")\n\n# Example 2: Invalid input\ninvalid_numbers = []\ntry:\n    controller.compute(invalid_numbers)\nexcept ValidationError as e:\n    print(f\"Error: {e.message}\") # Expected: Input list must be non-empty.\n\n# Example 3: Get metrics\nmetrics = controller.get_metrics()\nprint(f\"Current metrics: {metrics}\")\n```\n\n### 3.2. CLI Mode\n\nAfter installation, the `even-at-odd` command will be available.\n\n**Using space-separated integers:**\n\n```bash\npoetry run even-at-odd compute 4 2 6 7\n# Output: 2\n\npoetry run even-at-odd compute 1 3 5 7\n# Output: 0\n```\n\n**Using a JSON list string:**\n\n```bash\npoetry run even-at-odd compute '[10, 20, 30, 40]'\n# Output: 20 + 40 = 60\n```\n\n**Reading from STDIN:**\n\n```bash\necho \"4 2 6 7\" | poetry run even-at-odd compute\n# Output: 2\n\necho \"[10, 20, 30, 40]\" | poetry run even-at-odd compute\n# Output: 60\n```\n\n**Error Handling in CLI:**\n\n```bash\npoetry run even-at-odd compute\n# Error: Invalid input - Input list must be non-empty.\n# (Exits with non-zero code)\n\npoetry run even-at-odd compute 1 2 \"hello\" 4\n# Error: Invalid input - All items in the list must be integers. Found non-integer at index 2: hello.\n```\n\n### 3.3. HTTP API Mode\n\nThe API runs using Uvicorn.\n\n**Start the API server:**\n\n```bash\n# This uses the `app` instance exposed by __init__.py\npoetry run uvicorn even_at_odd:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload\n```\nThe API will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.\n\n**Endpoints:**\n\n-   **POST `/compute`**: Calculates the sum.\n    -   **Request Body (JSON):**\n        ```json\n        {\n            \"numbers\": [4, 2, 6, 7]\n        }\n        ```\n    -   **Response (JSON - 200 OK):**\n        ```json\n        {\n            \"result\": 2\n        }\n        ```\n    -   **Example with `curl`:**\n        ```bash\n        curl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"numbers\": [4, 2, 6, 7]}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/compute\n        # Output: {\"result\":2}\n        ```\n\n-   **GET `/metrics`**: Retrieves basic invocation metrics.\n    -   **Response (JSON - 200 OK):**\n        ```json\n        {\n            \"invocation_count\": 1,\n            \"last_result\": 2\n        }\n        ```\n    -   **Example with `curl`:**\n        ```bash\n        curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/metrics\n        # Output: {\"invocation_count\":1,\"last_result\":2}\n        ```\n\n**API Key Authentication (Optional):**\n\nTo enable API key authentication, set the `EVEN_AT_ODD_API_KEY` environment variable before starting the server:\n\n```bash\nexport EVEN_AT_ODD_API_KEY=\"my_secret_api_key_123\"\npoetry run uvicorn even_at_odd:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload\n```\n\nThen, include the `X-API-KEY` header in your requests:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -H \"X-API-KEY: my_secret_api_key_123\" -d '{\"numbers\": [4, 2, 6, 7]}' http://127.0.0.1:8000/compute\n```\nWithout the correct API key, requests will receive a `401 Unauthorized` response.\n\n## 4. Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest tests/\n```\n\n### CI/CD\n\nA GitHub Actions workflow is set up to run linting and tests on pushes and pull requests.\n\n## 5. Project Structure\n\n```\n.\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 src/\n\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 even_at_odd/\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 __init__.py           # Package init, dependency injection setup, exposes CLI/API instances\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 even_odd_service.py   # Core logic for sum computation\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validator.py          # Input validation logic\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 controller.py         # Orchestrates validation, computation, and metrics\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 cli.py                # Command Line Interface implementation\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 api.py                # FastAPI application setup and endpoints\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 config.py             # Application configuration\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 metrics_repository.py # In-memory metrics storage\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 validation_error.py   # Custom exception for validation errors\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 input_dto.py          # Pydantic DTO for API request body\n\u2502       \u251c\u2500\u2500 result_dto.py         # Pydantic DTO for API response body\n\u2502       \u2514\u2500\u2500 utils.py              # Helper functions (e.g., string parsing)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 pyproject.toml                # Project metadata and dependencies (Poetry)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 README.md                     # Project overview and usage instructions\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 .github/\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500 workflows/\n        \u2514\u2500\u2500 ci.yml                # GitHub Actions CI pipeline\n```\n```\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/ci.yml\nname: Python CI\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches:\n      - main\n  pull_request:\n    branches:\n      - main\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n\n    steps:\n    - name: Checkout code\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v5\n      with:\n        python-version: '3.9' # Target Python version as per spec\n\n    - name: Install Poetry\n      run: pip install poetry\n\n    - name: Configure Poetry\n      run: poetry config virtualenvs.in-project true\n\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: poetry install --no-root\n\n    # The design spec forbids generating unit tests, so we omit the pytest step for now.\n    # If tests were allowed:\n    # - name: Run tests\n    #   run: poetry run pytest\n\n    - name: Lint with Flake8 (Optional, but good practice)\n      run: |\n        poetry run pip install flake8\n        poetry run flake8 src/even_at_odd/ --count --select=E9,F63,F7,F82 --show-source --statistics\n        poetry run flake8 src/even_at_odd/ --count --exit-zero --max-complexity=10 --max-line-length=120 --statistics\n```"}
