{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "```python\ndef get_row(lst, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds occurrences of integer x in a jagged list and returns their coordinates.\n    Coordinates are sorted by row ascending, then by column descending within each row.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_coordinates = []\n    for row_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        # Collect column indices for target x in the current row\n        current_row_matches = []\n        for col_idx, value in enumerate(row):\n            if value == x:\n                current_row_matches.append(col_idx)\n        \n        # Sort collected column indices in descending order as required\n        current_row_matches.sort(reverse=True)\n        \n        # Append coordinates for this row to the main result list\n        for col in current_row_matches:\n            result_coordinates.append((row_idx, col))\n            \n    return result_coordinates\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting.\n    Sort ascending if sum(first, last) is odd; sort descending if sum(first, last) is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy to ensure the original array is not modified.\n    arr_copy = list(array)\n\n    first_element = arr_copy[0]\n    last_element = arr_copy[-1]\n\n    # Determine sorting order based on the parity of the sum of first and last elements.\n    if (first_element + last_element) % 2 == 1:\n        return sorted(arr_copy)  # Ascending sort for odd sum.\n    else:\n        return sorted(arr_copy, reverse=True)  # Descending sort for even sum.\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "def sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts an array of non-negative integers based on the parity of the sum of its first and last elements.\n    Returns a sorted copy, leaving the original array unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return []\n    \n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    first_last_sum = array[0] + array[-1]\n\n    if first_last_sum % 2 == 1:  # Odd sum, sort ascending\n        return sorted(array)\n    else:  # Even sum, sort descending\n        return sorted(array, reverse=True)"}
