{"task_id": "HumanEval/95", "solution": "```python\ndef check_dict_case(dict):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a dictionary, return True if all keys are strings in lower \n    case or all keys are strings in upper case, else return False.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not dict:\n        return False\n\n    keys = list(dict.keys())\n\n    # Check if all keys are strings.\n    if not all(isinstance(key, str) for key in keys):\n        return False\n\n    # Check if all keys are lowercase or all keys are uppercase.\n    all_lower = all(key == key.lower() for key in keys)\n    all_upper = all(key == key.upper() for key in keys)\n\n    return all_lower or all_upper\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "```python\ndef count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement a function that takes an non-negative integer and returns an array of the first n\n    integers that are prime numbers and less than n.\n    for example:\n    count_up_to(5) => [2,3]\n    count_up_to(11) => [2,3,5,7]\n    count_up_to(0) => []\n    count_up_to(20) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19]\n    count_up_to(1) => []\n    count_up_to(18) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17]\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize sieve: sieve[i] is True if i is potentially prime.\n    sieve = [True] * n\n    sieve[0], sieve[1] = False, False # Mark 0 and 1 as not prime.\n\n    p = 2\n    while p * p < n:\n        if sieve[p]: # If p is prime, mark its multiples as not prime.\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                sieve[multiple] = False\n        p += 1\n\n    # Collect all numbers where sieve[i] is True.\n    primes = []\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if sieve[i]:\n            primes.append(i)\n\n    return primes\n```"}
