{"task_id": "HumanEval/135", "solution": "def can_arrange(arr):\n    \"\"\"Returns the largest index of an element that is less than its predecessor.\n    If no such element exists, returns -1.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, 0, -1):\n        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            return i\n    return -1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "To generate the code according to the detailed software design specification, the following files will be created within the `src/last_char_checker/` directory, along with `pyproject.toml` and `README.md` at the project root. This implementation fully adheres to the modular, layered architecture, error handling, persistence, and API/CLI requirements outlined in the design specification, including reconciling the core logic to match all provided examples.\n\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/config.py\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Determine a cross-platform default path for the database.\n# On Linux/macOS: ~/.local/share/last_char_checker/checks.db\n# On Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%/last_char_checker/checks.db\nif os.name == 'posix':  # Linux, macOS, Unix\n    _base_dir = Path.home() / \".local\" / \"share\" / \"last_char_checker\"\nelif os.name == 'nt':  # Windows\n    _base_dir = Path(os.environ.get('LOCALAPPDATA', Path.home() / 'AppData' / 'Local')) / \"last_char_checker\"\nelse: # Fallback for other OS or if LOCALAPPDATA not set\n    _base_dir = Path.home() / \".last_char_checker\"\n\nDEFAULT_DB_PATH: str = str(_base_dir / \"checks.db\")\nMAX_INPUT_LENGTH: int = 10000\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/exceptions.py\nclass TextCheckError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for validation and business logic errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/text_input.py\nclass TextInput:\n    \"\"\"A simple data class to encapsulate input text.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, text: str) -> None:\n        self.text: str = text\n\n    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n        return f\"TextInput(text={self.text!r})\"\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/dto.py\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any\n\nclass CheckResultDTO:\n    \"\"\"Data Transfer Object for check results, including persistence info.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, result: bool, message: Optional[str] = None, record_id: Optional[int] = None) -> None:\n        self.result = result\n        self.message = message\n        self.record_id = record_id\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Convert DTO attributes to a dictionary.\"\"\"\n        return {\"result\": self.result, \"message\": self.message, \"record_id\": self.record_id}\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/utils.py\nimport datetime\n\ndef safe_truncate(text: str, n: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Truncate text to a maximum length, adding ellipsis if truncated.\"\"\"\n    if text is None:\n        return \"\"\n    if len(text) > n:\n        return text[:n-3] + \"...\" if n > 3 else text[:n]\n    return text\n\ndef now_iso() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return current UTC time in ISO 8601 format.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec='seconds')\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/validator.py\nfrom .exceptions import TextCheckError\nfrom .config import MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\n\nclass TextValidator:\n    \"\"\"Validates input text for type and length constraints.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, max_length: int = MAX_INPUT_LENGTH) -> None:\n        self._max_length = max_length\n\n    def validate(self, text: str) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Raises TextCheckError if input is invalid.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(text, str):\n            raise TextCheckError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n        if len(text) > self._max_length:\n            raise TextCheckError(f\"Input exceeds maximum length of {self._max_length} characters.\")\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/repository.py\nimport sqlite3\nimport os\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_DB_PATH\nfrom .utils import safe_truncate, now_iso\n\nclass TestCaseRepository:\n    \"\"\"Manages persistence of check results in a local SQLite database.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = DEFAULT_DB_PATH) -> None:\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n\n    def initialize(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the database connection and creates tables if they don't exist.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is not None:\n            return\n\n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self._db_path), exist_ok=True)\n        self._conn = sqlite3.connect(self._db_path, check_same_thread=False)\n        self._conn.execute(\"PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;\")\n        self._conn.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;\")\n\n        cur = self._conn.cursor()\n        cur.execute(\"\"\"\n        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS checks (\n          id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n          input_text TEXT NOT NULL,\n          result INTEGER NOT NULL, -- 0 for False, 1 for True\n          error TEXT NULL,\n          created_at TEXT NOT NULL -- ISO8601 timestamp\n        )\"\"\")\n        cur.execute(\"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_checks_created_at ON checks(created_at DESC)\")\n        self._conn.commit()\n\n    def insert(self, text: str, result: bool, error: Optional[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Inserts a new check record into the database, truncating input/error if too long.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            self.initialize()\n        \n        truncated_text = safe_truncate(text, 1000)\n        truncated_error = safe_truncate(error, 500) if error else None\n\n        cur = self._conn.cursor()\n        cur.execute(\"INSERT INTO checks (input_text, result, error, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                    (truncated_text, int(result), truncated_error, now_iso()))\n        self._conn.commit()\n        return cur.lastrowid\n\n    def query_recent(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Queries and returns a list of recent check records.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            self.initialize()\n        cur = self._conn.cursor()\n        cur.execute(\"SELECT id, input_text, result, error, created_at FROM checks ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?\", (limit,))\n        rows = cur.fetchall()\n        \n        columns = [description[0] for description in cur.description]\n        return [dict(zip(columns, row)) for row in rows]\n\n    def close(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Closes the database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn:\n            self._conn.close()\n            self._conn = None\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/last_char_checker_service.py\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom .dto import CheckResultDTO\nfrom .exceptions import TextCheckError\nfrom .validator import TextValidator\nfrom .repository import TestCaseRepository\n\nclass LastCharCheckerService:\n    \"\"\"Core service for checking the last character rule, orchestrating validation and persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: TestCaseRepository, validator: TextValidator) -> None:\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def check(self, text: str) -> CheckResultDTO:\n        \"\"\"Validates input, computes the check result, persists it, and returns a DTO.\"\"\"\n        record_id: Optional[int] = None\n        error_message: Optional[str] = None\n        result: bool = False # Default result in case of validation error\n\n        try:\n            self._validator.validate(text)\n            result = self._is_last_char_standalone_letter(text)\n            record_id = self._repo.insert(text, result, None)\n            return CheckResultDTO(result=result, message=None, record_id=record_id)\n        except TextCheckError as e:\n            error_message = str(e)\n            try: # Attempt to persist the error, but don't fail the service if repo has issues\n                record_id = self._repo.insert(text, False, error_message)\n            except Exception as repo_exc:\n                error_message += f\" (Persistence failed: {repo_exc})\"\n            return CheckResultDTO(result=False, message=error_message, record_id=record_id)\n        except Exception as e:\n            error_message = f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\"\n            try:\n                record_id = self._repo.insert(text, False, error_message)\n            except Exception: # Ignore repo exception if already handling another error\n                pass\n            return CheckResultDTO(result=False, message=error_message, record_id=record_id)\n\n    def _is_last_char_standalone_letter(self, text: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the last character is an isolated alphabetical character.\n        This internal method implements the core business logic from FR1 and examples.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not text: # Handles \"\" \u279e False\n            return False\n\n        if text[-1] == ' ': # Handles \"apple pi e \" \u279e False (original string ends with space)\n            return False\n\n        # At this point, `text` is not empty and does not end with a space.\n        # Apply FR1's core logic: \"last char is letter and previous char is a space (or string length==1)\".\n        last_char = text[-1]\n\n        if not last_char.isalpha(): # If last char is not a letter \u279e False\n            return False\n\n        if len(text) == 1: # If string length is 1 and it's a letter \u279e True (e.g., \"a\" \u279e True)\n            return True\n\n        # If previous char is a space \u279e True (e.g., \" pi e\" \u279e True).\n        return text[-2] == ' '\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/controller.py\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .last_char_checker_service import LastCharCheckerService\nfrom .dto import CheckResultDTO\nfrom .exceptions import TextCheckError\nfrom .repository import TestCaseRepository\nfrom .validator import TextValidator\nfrom .config import DEFAULT_DB_PATH, MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface parsing, execution, and user output.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: LastCharCheckerService) -> None:\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the CLI command based on provided arguments.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            prog=\"lastcharcheck\",\n            description=\"Checks if the last character of a string is an isolated letter.\"\n        )\n        parser.add_argument(\n            \"text\",\n            type=str,\n            help=\"The input string to check.\"\n        )\n\n        try:\n            args = parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n        except SystemExit as e:\n            return e.code # argparse prints help/error and exits, capture its exit code\n\n        text_to_check = args.text\n        \n        dto: CheckResultDTO\n        try:\n            dto = self._service.check(text_to_check)\n            if dto.message:\n                # Print informational or error messages from the service.\n                print(f\"Info/Error: {dto.message}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            \n            # Print the primary boolean result to stdout.\n            print(\"True\" if dto.result else \"False\")\n            \n            # Return non-zero for explicit TextCheckErrors, otherwise 0.\n            if dto.message and not dto.result and \"Input\" in dto.message:\n                return 1 # Validation errors result in exit code 1\n            return 0 # Success exit code for normal operation or non-critical issues\n        except Exception as e:\n            # Catch any unexpected system-level errors.\n            print(f\"An unexpected system error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Generic error exit code\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Main function for the lastcharcheck CLI entry point.\"\"\"\n    # Initialize dependencies\n    repo = TestCaseRepository(db_path=DEFAULT_DB_PATH)\n    validator = TextValidator(max_length=MAX_INPUT_LENGTH)\n    service = LastCharCheckerService(repo=repo, validator=validator)\n    controller = CLIController(service=service)\n\n    # Run the controller with command line arguments\n    exit_code = controller.run(sys.argv)\n    \n    # Ensure the repository connection is closed\n    repo.close() \n\n    sys.exit(exit_code)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/last_char_checker/__init__.py\n# Expose the public API of the library.\nfrom .last_char_checker_service import LastCharCheckerService\nfrom .repository import TestCaseRepository\nfrom .validator import TextValidator\nfrom .exceptions import TextCheckError\nfrom .dto import CheckResultDTO\nfrom .config import MAX_INPUT_LENGTH, DEFAULT_DB_PATH\n\n# Define __all__ for explicit exports when `from last_char_checker import *` is used.\n__all__ = [\n    \"LastCharCheckerService\",\n    \"TestCaseRepository\",\n    \"TextValidator\",\n    \"TextCheckError\",\n    \"CheckResultDTO\",\n    \"MAX_INPUT_LENGTH\",\n    \"DEFAULT_DB_PATH\",\n]\n\n```\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"last-char-checker\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nauthors = [\n  { name=\"Your Name\", email=\"your.email@example.com\" }, # Replace with actual author info\n]\ndescription = \"A Python library and CLI to check if the last character of a string is an isolated letter.\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nlicense = { text = \"MIT\" } # Specify license for project\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Operating System :: OS Independent\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"Topic :: Software Development :: Libraries\",\n    \"Topic :: Utilities\",\n]\ndependencies = [\n    # No external runtime dependencies specified beyond standard library and system defaults.\n]\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/yourusername/last-char-checker\" # Replace with actual repo URL\n\"Bug Tracker\" = \"https://github.com/yourusername/last-char-checker/issues\" # Replace with actual bug tracker URL\n\n[project.scripts]\nlastcharcheck = \"last_char_checker.controller:main\" # Defines the CLI entrypoint\n\n```\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# Last Char Checker\n\nA Python library and command-line interface (CLI) tool to evaluate if the last character of a given string is an isolated alphabetical character.\n\n## Features\n\n-   **Core Logic**: Checks if the last character is a letter and is separated by a space (or is the only character).\n-   **CLI**: `lastcharcheck \"some string\"` for quick interactive use.\n-   **Programmatic API**: `LastCharCheckerService.check()` for integration into other Python systems.\n-   **Persistence**: Logs all checks and results to a local SQLite database for auditing and debugging.\n-   **Robustness**: Input validation, error handling, and modular design following SOLID principles.\n\n## Installation\n\nYou can install `last-char-checker` by cloning the repository and installing locally:\n\n```bash\n# Assuming you are in the directory containing pyproject.toml\ngit clone https://github.com/yourusername/last-char-checker.git\ncd last-char-checker\npip install .\n```\n\nTo enable shell autocompletion for the CLI (e.g., for `bash`), you might need to follow specific instructions for your shell after installation, often involving `argcomplete`.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nTo check a string from your terminal:\n\n```bash\nlastcharcheck \"apple pi e\"\n# Output: True\n\nlastcharcheck \"apple pie\"\n# Output: False\n\nlastcharcheck \"apple pi e \"\n# Output: False\n\nlastcharcheck \"\"\n# Output: False\n\nlastcharcheck \"a\"\n# Output: True\n\nlastcharcheck \" a\"\n# Output: True\n\nlastcharcheck \"a \"\n# Output: False\n\nlastcharcheck \"this is too long and will exceed the default max length of 10000 characters if you type enough text here.........................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................................