{"task_id": "HumanEval/137", "solution": "```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\ndef compare_one(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two numeric values (int, float, or strings representing real numbers)\n    and returns the larger value preserving its original variable type.\n    Returns None if the values are numerically equal.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Process 'a' to get its Decimal representation\n    a_decimal_val = None\n    if isinstance(a, int):\n        a_decimal_val = Decimal(a)\n    elif isinstance(a, float):\n        # Use Decimal.from_float for precise conversion of binary floats.\n        a_decimal_val = Decimal.from_float(a)\n    elif isinstance(a, str):\n        s_a = a.strip()\n        # Normalize comma decimal separator to dot if no dot is present.\n        if ',' in s_a and '.' not in s_a:\n            s_a = s_a.replace(',', '.')\n        # Convert string to Decimal, trusting the input is a valid numeric string.\n        a_decimal_val = Decimal(s_a)\n\n    # Process 'b' to get its Decimal representation\n    b_decimal_val = None\n    if isinstance(b, int):\n        b_decimal_val = Decimal(b)\n    elif isinstance(b, float):\n        # Use Decimal.from_float for precise conversion of binary floats.\n        b_decimal_val = Decimal.from_float(b)\n    elif isinstance(b, str):\n        s_b = b.strip()\n        # Normalize comma decimal separator to dot if no dot is present.\n        if ',' in s_b and '.' not in s_b:\n            s_b = s_b.replace(',', '.')\n        # Convert string to Decimal, trusting the input is a valid numeric string.\n        b_decimal_val = Decimal(s_b)\n\n    # Compare the Decimal values and return the original input or None\n    if a_decimal_val > b_decimal_val:\n        return a\n    elif b_decimal_val > a_decimal_val:\n        return b\n    else:  # Values are numerically equal\n        return None\n```"}
