{"task_id": "HumanEval/151", "solution": "```python\ndef double_the_difference(lst):\n    '''\n    Given a list of numbers, return the sum of squares of the numbers\n    in the list that are odd. Ignore numbers that are negative or not integers.\n    '''\n    total = 0\n    for n in lst:\n        # Consider only non-negative, whole numbers (integers or floats like 3.0).\n        # This implicitly handles non-integers like 3.5, and negative numbers.\n        if n >= 0 and n == int(n):\n            integer_value = int(n)\n            # Check if the integer value is odd.\n            if integer_value % 2 != 0:\n                total += integer_value * integer_value\n    return total\n```"}
